\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10512\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2025 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin analyst 'highly doubts' return to $50K \u8212\'20\'14 Will the weekly close spark a correction?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 All eyes on the weekly close for Bitcoin as BTC price action nears historical resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) challenged brand-new support levels on Oct. 14 after overnight successes took the market past $58,000\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/50fc54a0-dd80-42ea-b13c-91d192913da2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin "dips" to near $57,000\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  tracked BTC/USD as it reversed towards $57,000 after hitting highs of $58,540 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The moves mimicked the first time Bitcoin had attacked $58,000 in February \u8212\'20\'14 several attempts interspersed by consolidation, followed ultimately by a run to April's all-time highs.\par \par \uc2 Despite on-chain indicators showing that Bitcoin is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-eyes-big-58k-resistance-as-new-data-shows-hodlers-acting-the-opposite-to-q1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 different beast}}}\uc2  in Q4, however, the mood was just as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time around.\par \par \uc2 "Bitcoin is most likely just continuing this grind towards the all-time highs," Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cryptomichnl/status/1448555039585443843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in his latest \uc2 Twitter\uc2  update.\par \par \uc2 "Great bounce from $54K. Highly doubt we'll see a retest at $50K happening."\par \par \uc2 Cementing $50,000 as support \u8212\'20\'14 albeit for a second time in 2021 \u8212\'20\'14 would form a clear signal on the market trajectory as pundits gear up for what they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/catch-the-bitcoin-dip-btc-price-pares-losses-with-a-fresh-surge-to-57k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expect}}}\uc2  to be an explosive end to the year.\par \par \uc2 For trader and analyst Rekt Capital, however, there was potential cause for concern this week. Zooming out, BTC/USD has failed to close a weekly candle above $60,000, and a repeat performance could likewise spell a copycat correction\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  has successfully retested its Daily Bull Flag thus far\par \par \uc2 But Bitcoin is still below major Weekly resistance (red)\par \par \uc2 In fact, any sort of Weekly Close below $60000 has historically preceded a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  retrace from these highs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n9vFaaalVM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n9vFaaalVM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rekt Capital (@rektcapital) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rektcapital/status/1448338538102149131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 13, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 That leaves bulls until Sunday to crack a historical watermark, something which may still be helped before Monday's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-tickers-and-ark-filing-shows-bitcoin-futures-etf-approval-imminent-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approval decision}}}\uc2  on a futures-based exchange-traded fund (ETF).\par \par \uc2 Polkadot breakout headlines altcoin return\par \par \uc2 Altcoins meanwhile saw brief respite from weakness in the face of "Bitcoin Season."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-10-13-btc-eth-bnb-ada-xrp-sol-doge-dot-luna-uni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 10/13: BTC, ETH, BNB, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI}}}\par \par \uc2 The exception was Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ), up 28% in a week on news that its auctions would finally begin next month \u8212\'20\'14 a key original feature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/polkadot-to-debut-parachain-auctions-after-governance-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five years}}}\uc2  in the making.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5b750651-6caf-4406-91d8-a7e882426a67.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USD 1-hour candle chart (Kraken). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The largest altcoin Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) managed 5.3% daily gains, with all of the top ten cryptocurrencies by market cap trading higher on the day as Bitcoin slowed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZTBmOWZiYmQtYWU1Mi00NzI3LWI2MzktMzllZmVhNzRhY2RlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211014ehae0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/13: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin remains strong above its recent breakout level, but several major altcoins are still under pressure until BTC reveals its next move.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has been sustaining above $54,000 for the past few days but that has not resulted in euphoria among investors. Google Trends data shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-search-interest-nears-1-year-lows-as-btc-price-slips-below-55k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin search interest has not picked up}}}\uc2  in recent days and is nearing one-year lows. Some analysts believe that this is a sign that only stronger hands are accumulating.\par \par \uc2 A recent report from \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  also showed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-crypto-products-eye-record-aum-as-investors-pile-into-bitcoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional investors pumped more than $226 million}}}\uc2  into Bitcoin products in the week ending Oct. 8. The analysis firm estimates that the total assets under the management of institutional crypto products have ballooned to $66.7 billion, just 5% below the record hit in May.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c28e1bb9-a7a0-4c8c-8b65-a777171559ba.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Data from Glassnode also shows that the Bitcoin wallets of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/long-term-bitcoin-bulls-hodl-strong-despite-five-month-price-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long-term holders contain 13.3 million Bitcoin}}}\uc2 , accounting for 70% of the entire Bitcoin supply. The long-term holders have not sold their holdings and have also added more than 2.37 million Bitcoin to their wallets over the past seven months. Bitcoin purchasing by long-term whales outstrips newly mined coins by 12.7 times, the report added.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin continue its up-move or is it time for a few days of consolidation? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin turned down from $57,680 on Oct. 12 but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests buying on dips. The bears again tried to pull the price below the breakout level at $52,920 but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates that bulls are not relenting.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/2b6f2849-a335-4d6e-a392-fe70993dd2ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The rising 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($51,338) and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive zone indicate an advantage to buyers. If bulls drive the price above $57,839.04, the BTC/USDT pair could rally to $60,000.\par \par \uc2 This level may act as a tough resistance but if bulls push the price above it, the pair could retest the all-time high at $64,854. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may pick up if bulls overcome this obstacle.\par \par \uc2 The breakout level at $52,920 remains the key support to watch on the downside. A break below this level and the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that bulls may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) has rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($3,390) for the past three days, indicating that bulls are accumulating on dips. The bulls will now try to push the price to the neckline of the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e8453eb9-a3b6-4ba1-a052-cc387424e64f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the neckline will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup, which has a target objective of $4,657. The gradually rising 20-day EMA and the RSI above 55 indicate a modest advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 However, the rally may not be linear as the ETH/USDT pair could face stiff resistance at $4,027.88 and later at $4,372.72.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the neckline and breaks below the moving averages, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to $3,160 and later to the psychological support at $3,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the 20-day EMA ($417) on Oct. 10 but the bears could not build on this advantage. The bulls defended the psychological support at $400 and pushed the price back above the 20-day EMA on Oct. 11.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/2d13de9a-cce0-43db-a9b8-492d30702caf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although bears pulled the price below $400 on Oct. 12, the move appears to have been a bear trap because the BNB/USDT pair recovered quickly and rebounded to the neckline. The buyers pushed the price above the neckline on Oct. 13.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse H&S pattern will complete if the pair closes above the neckline. This setup could start an up-move to $519.90 where heavy opposition is expected.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this level could propel the pair to the pattern target at $554. The bears will have to pull the price below $392.20 to gain the upper hand.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the support line of the symmetrical triangle on Oct. 12. This suggests that the uncertainty of the past few days has resolved in favor of the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/42cd1592-fa79-4bcd-a3ff-7935fcc19e23.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price back above the 20-day EMA ($2.21) but if they fail, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to $1.87. This is a critical level to monitor because if it breaks down, the decline may extend to $1.63.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has dropped below 44, indicating advantage to bears. This negative perspective will be invalidated if bulls push and sustain the pair above the resistance line of the triangle.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($1.06) on Oct. 12 but the bulls are finding it difficult to sustain the price above the 50-day simple moving average ($1.08). This suggests a lack of buyers at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/16721080-4813-44de-8e72-e3cbf7ed9bd7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears sink and sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to the psychological support at $1. A break and close below this level could intensify selling and sink the pair to $0.85.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above the overhead resistance at $1.24. If they manage to do that, the pair could rally to $1.41.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) broke below the 50-day SMA ($144) on Oct. 12 but bears could not capitalize on this weakness. The bulls bought the dip aggressively and pushed the price back to the 20-day EMA ($151) on the same day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/6bb501eb-12da-4ad0-b754-7f25390aa685.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The SOL/USDT pair rose modestly above the 20-day EMA today but strong selling by the bears has pulled the price back to the 50-day SMA. If bears sink and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA, the decline could extend to $116.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the downtrend line. The pair could then climb to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80. A break and close above this level could pave the way for a rally to $200.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE)}}}\uc2  broke below the 20-day EMA ($0.23) on Oct. 10 and the bulls have not been able to reclaim the level since then. This suggests that bears are putting up a strong defense at the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/01a48200-c0b3-491a-bedd-eb003e5c6b36.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair could drop to $0.21 and if this support cracks, the next stop could be $0.19. This level has acted as astrong support during the previous two occasions; hence, bulls may again defend it with vigor.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from the current level and rises above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rally to the downtrend line. A break and close above this resistance will indicate the possible end of the down move.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/2021/10/13/crypto-scoring-big-with-european-football"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto scoring big with European football}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) bounced off the 20-day EMA ($33.02) on Oct. 12, indicating that the sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips. The bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance at $38.77 where bears are expected to mount stiff resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1763eb3f-56de-46f5-9648-b80d134b27ff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $38.77, the DOT/USDT pair could again drop to the moving averages. This is an important support for bulls to defend because a break below the 50-day SMA ($31.37) could open the doors for a decline to $25.50.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price continues to rise from the current level and breaks above $38.77, the uptrend could resume. The first target on the upside is the all-time high at $49.78 and then the pattern target at $52.04.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token dropped to the 50-day SMA ($35.87) on Oct. 12 but the bulls bought this dip as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The buyers tried to push the price back above the 20-day EMA ($39.15) on Oct. 13 but failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/eabb631f-77e7-4e36-aff1-ac2773474102.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI has slipped below the midpoint, indicating that bulls may be losing their grip. If bears pull and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA, the LUNA/USDT pair could drop to $32.50.\par \par \uc2 This level could act as a strong support but if it cracks, the selling could intensify and the pair may plummet to $25. Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the current level and rises above the 20-day EMA, the bulls may push the pair to $45.01.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) bounced off the strong support at $22 on Oct. 12 and bulls pushed the price above the moving averages on Oct. 13. However, the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c85c70f5-3071-4d85-824f-37e73187f7b5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($24.29) is flat and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. A break and close below $22 could tilt the advantage in favor of bears. The UNI/USDT pair could then drop to $18.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rises from the current level and breaks above the neckline of the inverted H&S pattern, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up. The pair could first rally to $31.41 and then march toward the pattern target at $36.98.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZjBlZDNiZjYtZTJhYS00N2Y2LWI2OWUtZWNjYWY1NWUxNzdkLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211013ehad000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional crypto products eye record AUM as investors pile into Bitcoin\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 387 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has firmly reclaimed its dominance over flows to institutional crypto products while investors reduce Ether exposure.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors are continuing to pile into Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) despite prices pushing up to a five-month high.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Tuesday \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-50-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-75707f4ec02f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , more than $226 million in capital flowed to institutional Bitcoin products this past week. Bitcoin products dominated inflows for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-bulls-back-bitcoin-after-weeks-of-altcoin-accumulation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third consecutive week}}}\uc2 , posting a week-over-week increase of 227%.\par \par \uc2 The heavy inflows coincided with the price of BTC gaining 12.5% for the week, with BTC sitting at around $54,000 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  attributes the positive shift in sentiment toward Bitcoin to recent statements from United States Securities and Exchange Commission Chairman Gary Gensler suggesting the long-awaited approval of the U.S.\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-56k-as-bulls-return-and-talk-focuses-on-bitcoin-etf-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Bitcoin exchange-traded fund}}}\uc2  (ETF) may be just around the corner.\par \par \uc2 The surging activity surrounding Bitcoin has seen the combined assets under management (AUM) of institutional crypto products push up to $66.7 billion last week \u8212\'20\'14 with \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  estimating the total is just 5% shy of the sector\u8217\'20\'19s record AUM from May.\par \par \uc2 Products tracking altcoins have posted mixed performances for the week, with Solana (SOL) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) products generating inflows of $12.5 million and $3 million, respectively. However, funds offering exposure to Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  suffered outflows of $13.6 million, $2.1 million and $600,000, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment products have now posted inflows for eight weeks in a row.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/billionaire-bill-miller-advocates-for-bitcoin-but-doubtful-on-altcoins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Billionaire Bill Miller advocates for Bitcoin, but doubtful on altcoins}}}\par \par \uc2 Many onlookers are attributing BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-57k-five-month-high-5-things-to-watch-in-btc-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  momentum}}}\uc2  to expectations that the SEC will soon approve a futures-based \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the SEC has previously shot down every application it has received for physically backed Bitcoin ETFs, the SEC is currently deliberating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/currencies/bitcoin-futures-etf-cryptocurrency-sec-exchange-traded-fund-gary-gensler-2021-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four}}}\uc2  applications for exchange-traded funds based on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange\u8217\'20\'19s (CME) regulated futures contracts.\par \par \uc2 With CME\u8217\'20\'19s futures markets offering a product that is already insured and overseen by U.S. regulators, pundits such as senior ETF analyst for Bloomberg Eric Balchunas believe that Bitcoin futures ETFs are \u8220\'20\'1Clikely on schedule\u8221\'20\'1D to receive a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/futures-based-bitcoin-etf-has-75-chance-of-approval-in-october-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulatory green light}}}\uc2  this month.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvN2M4NDU0ZGQtYTY3NS00MTA1LWFiNGItNmVkYmQ0YjNjOWNmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211012ehac0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional crypto products eye record AUM as investors pile into Bitcoin\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 393 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has firmly reclaimed its dominance over flows to institutional crypto products while investors reduce Ether exposure.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors are continuing to pile into Bitcoin despite prices pushing up to a five-month high.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Oct. 12 \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-50-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-75707f4ec02f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , more than $226 million in capital flowed to institutional Bitcoin (BTC) products this past week. Bitcoin products dominated inflows for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-bulls-back-bitcoin-after-weeks-of-altcoin-accumulation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 third consecutive week}}}\uc2 , posting a week-over-week increase of 227%.\par \par \uc2 The heavy inflows coincided with the price of BTC gaining 12.5% for the week, with BTC sitting at around $54,000 on Oct. 8.\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  attributes the positive shift in sentiment towards Bitcoin to recent statements from U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) chairman Gary Gensler\u8217\'20\'19s suggesting the long-awaited approval of the United States\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-56k-as-bulls-return-and-talk-focuses-on-bitcoin-etf-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Bitcoin exchange-traded fund}}}\uc2  (ETF) may be just around the corner.\par \par \uc2 The surging activity surrounding Bitcoin has seen the combined assets under management (AUM) of institutional crypto products push up to $66.7 billion last week \u8212\'20\'14 with \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  estimating the total is just 5% shy of the sector\u8217\'20\'19s record AUM from May.\par \par \uc2 Products tracking altcoins have posted a mixed performance for the week, with Solana (SOL) and Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) products generating inflows of $12.5 million and $3 million respectively. However, funds offering exposure to Ether (ETH), Polkadot (DOT) and Ripple (XRP) suffered outflows of $13.6 million, $2.1 million and $600,000 each.\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment products have now posted inflows for eight weeks in a row.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/billionaire-bill-miller-advocates-for-bitcoin-but-doubtful-on-altcoins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Billionaire Bill Miller advocates for Bitcoin, but doubtful on altcoins}}}\par \par \uc2 Many onlookers are attributing BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-57k-five-month-high-5-things-to-watch-in-btc-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  momentum}}}\uc2  to expectations that the SEC will soon approve a futures-based \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While the SEC has previously shot down every application it has received for physically-backed Bitcoin ETFs, the SEC is currently deliberating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://markets.businessinsider.com/news/currencies/bitcoin-futures-etf-cryptocurrency-sec-exchange-traded-fund-gary-gensler-2021-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four}}}\uc2  applications for exchange-traded funds based on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange's (CME) regulated futures contracts.\par \par \uc2 With CME\u8217\'20\'19s futures markets offering a product that is already insured and overseen by U.S. regulators, pundits such as senior ETF analyst for Bloomberg Eric Balchunas believe that Bitcoin futures ETFs are \u8220\'20\'1Clikely on schedule\u8221\'20\'1D to receive a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/futures-based-bitcoin-etf-has-75-chance-of-approval-in-october-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulatory green light}}}\uc2  this month.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvN2M4NDU0ZGQtYTY3NS00MTA1LWFiNGItNmVkYmQ0YjNjOWNmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211012ehac00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/11: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Analysts say Bitcoin has started its journey toward a new all-time high and the sideways action from altcoins suggests traders are shifting funds into BTC.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) resumed its rally on Oct. 11 and climbed close to $58,000. This marks an almost 100% recovery from the May plunge and shows that any regulatory action by China is having only a temporary effect.\par \par \uc2 The strong rally in Bitcoin in the past few days has boosted sentiment and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-100k-price-target-returns-as-btc-price-breaks-out-of-bull-pennant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysts are back with their six-figure projections}}}\uc2 . Geoffrey Kendrick, head of emerging market currency research at Standard Chartered, anticipates Bitcoin to rally to $100,000 by early next year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/edc027b1-06cf-42e1-9e63-6ff8f7f21887.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 David Gokhshtein, the founder of Gokhshtein Media and PAC Global, was even more \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as he expects Bitcoin to reach $100,000 before the end of the year. Analyst and trader Rekt Capital believes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-passes-57-4k-in-a-fresh-surge-towards-february-resistance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin will rise much higher than $100,000}}}\uc2  in the current cycle.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin break above the stiff overhead resistance and challenge the all-time high and will altcoins play catch up? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s long wick on the Oct. 10 candlestick shows that bears sold at higher levels but their failure to pull the price below the breakout level at $52,920 seems to have energized the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/79d5b09a-b192-46ed-ae77-ed70bd822f14.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Aggressive buying on Oct. 11 has pushed the price above the Oct. 10 intraday high at $56,561.31, clearing the path for a possible rally to $60,000. The rising 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($50,196) and the relative strength index (RSI) in the overbought zone indicate that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 If bulls thrust the price above $60,000, the BTC/USDT pair could challenge the all-time high at $64,854. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up further if buyers clear this barrier.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the breakout level at $52,920. This will suggest that traders are booking profits at higher levels. The bears will then sense an opportunity and try to pull the price below the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($47,727).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down sharply on Oct. 10 but the bulls aggressively purchased the drop to the 20-day EMA ($3,369) on Oct. 11. This is a positive sign as it shows that the sentiment remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b1f779a2-813d-4769-b6b0-07777e9aeee3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls push and close the price above the neckline, the inverse head and shoulders (H&S) pattern will complete. This reversal setup has a pattern target at $4,657 but the bears are likely to have other plans as they will try to mount a strong resistance at $4,027.88 and then at the all-time high at $4,372.72.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be negated if the price turns down from the overhead resistance and plummets below the 50-day SMA ($3,351). The ETH/USDT pair could then drop to psychological support at $3,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the 50-day SMA ($425) on Oct. 8. The bulls tried to push the price back above the 50-day SMA on Oct. 9 but failed, inviting selling by short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/8eb84634-67ef-439a-a72a-7ba44433926c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The BNB/USDT pair plunged below the 20-day EMA ($409) on Oct. 10 but the bears could not take advantage of this opportunity. Strong buying at lower levels has pushed the price back above the 20-day EMA on Oct. 11.\par \par \uc2 If bulls propel the price above the 50-day SMA, the pair could rise to the neckline. A break and close above this level will complete the inverse H&S pattern. The pair may then rally to $518.90 and if this level is crossed, the rally may extend to the pattern target at $554.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA or the neckline and plunges below the 100-day SMA ($383), the next stop could be $320.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is trading inside a symmetrical triangle, which generally acts as a continuation pattern. If bears sink and sustain the price below the support line of the triangle, the correction could resume.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/4e7558eb-c8b5-4b27-9221-8270d793dc8e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA ($2.24) and the RSI just below the midpoint, do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. The bulls will try to arrest the decline at $1.94 but if they fail to do so, the selling could accelerate and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to $1.60.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the support line of the triangle and rises above the 20-day EMA, the bulls will try to push the pair above the resistance line of the triangle. If they succeed, the pair could rise to $2.47 and then rally to $2.80.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 The tight range trading in Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) resolved to the upside on Oct. 9 with a break and close above the 50-day SMA ($1.08). However, the long wick on the Oct. 10 candlestick shows that bears are defending the minor resistance at $1.24.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/7f4f566c-5e42-4ad8-89c3-6342b77879ca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls do not give up much ground from the current level, the possibility of a break above $1.24 increases. The 20-day EMA ($1.06) is sloping up marginally and the RSI is above 60, signaling advantage to buyers.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above $1.24 could push the XRP/USDT pair to $1.41. This may prove to be a difficult obstacle to overcome but if crossed, the pair could rally to $1.66. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA. That could pull the price down to $1 and then to the 100-day SMA ($0.93).\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana\u8217\'20\'19s (SOL) weak bounce off the 20-day EMA ($151) on Oct. 8 and 9 suggests a lack of aggressive buying by the bulls. Supply exceeded demand on Oct. 10 and the price slipped below the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c5516f52-0240-42b3-8077-2e6131e6d939.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to defend the 50-day SMA ($141). They will have to push and sustain the price above the downtrend line to signal that the selling pressure is easing. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up on a breakout and close above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and breaks below the 50-day SMA, the SOL/USDT pair could drop to the strong support at $116. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the pair could plummet to the 100-day SMA ($90).\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Although bulls defended the 100-day SMA ($0.24) on Oct. 8 and 9, they could not push \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the 50-day SMA ($0.24). This suggested that demand dries up at higher levels. The bears took advantage of this situation and pulled the price below the moving averages on Oct. 10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/90a51706-7806-4be4-a796-932a97421ab5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls fail to push the price back above the moving averages quickly, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to the $0.21 to $0.19 support zone. The bears will have to break this support zone to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up and breaks above the moving averages, the bulls will make another attempt to push the price above the downtrend line. If they pull it off, the pair could start an up-move $0.32 and later to $0.35.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/billionaire-bill-miller-advocates-for-bitcoin-but-doubtful-on-altcoins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Billionaire Bill Miller advocates for Bitcoin, but doubtful on altcoins}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) has been range-bound between $25.50 and $38.77 for the past many days. The price turned down from $37.45 on Oct. 10, suggesting that bears are defending the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e6c86e29-fb56-41a0-8712-7da09a0a48a7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The gradually upsloping moving averages and the RSI in the positive territory signal a modest edge to the buyers. A breakout and close above $38.77 will be the first sign of the resumption of the up-move.\par \par \uc2 The pattern target of the breakout from the rectangle pattern is $52.04. Alternatively, if bears sink the price below the moving averages, it will indicate that the DOT/USDT pair could extend its stay inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token turned down from $48.56 on Oct. 8, indicating that bears are aggressively defending the overhead resistance at $50. The failure to break above the resistance may have prompted short-term traders to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b0344c9b-9080-4d4a-b71b-03a5f2fbc8f6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LUNA/USDT pair slipped and closed below the 20-day EMA ($39.64) on Oct. 10. Efforts by the bulls to reclaim the level met with strong selling on Oct. 11, indicating that the sentiment has turned negative and traders are closing positions on every minor rally.\par \par \uc2 The next support on the downside is the 50-day SMA ($35.58) and if this level gives way, the decline could extend to $32.50. Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level and rises above the 20-day EMA, the bulls may again try to push the pair above the overhead resistance.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) broke and closed below the 20-day EMA ($24.45) on Oct. 10 but the bulls are trying to defend the 100-day SMA ($23.76). The buyers will now try to push the price back above the 50-day SMA ($25.05).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b61f5137-0cca-41b5-8435-ea1a6490acc8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the UNI/USDT pair could rise to the neckline of the inverted H&S pattern. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up if buyers push and sustain the price above this resistance. The pair could then begin its ascent toward the pattern target at $36.98.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if bears pull the price below the 100-day SMA, the pair could drop to $22. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it is breached, the selling could intensify and the pair may drop to $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvYjMyMzU0MDktMjQyZS00MWIyLWE3NzYtODY3ZjJlZGEzNGE5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211011ehab000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/8: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,787 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Profit-booking in Bitcoin and select altcoins may start a short-term correction.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) rally above $50,000 seems to have received a boost from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutions-buying-bitcoin-rather-than-gold-as-inflation-cranks-up-jpmorgan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional buyers who are looking to hedge}}}\uc2  their portfolio against increasing inflation, said \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in a note to its clients on Oct. 7. The bank\u8217\'20\'19s analysts speculated that institutional investors may be preferring Bitcoin over gold as a better hedge against inflation.\par \par \uc2 A recent study titled \u8220\'20\'1CCryptocurrencies and the Sharpe Ratio of Traditional Investment Models\u8221\'20\'1D by crypto asset management firms Iconic Funds and \uc2 Cryptology Asset Group\uc2  showed that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-exposure-has-positive-impact-on-investment-portfolios-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addition of cryptocurrencies to any portfolio improved returns}}}\uc2  and risk-reward performance of the portfolio.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e7d20fb9-b85d-4274-88e7-bc29a62ed0db.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg senior commodity strategist Mike McGlone said in the October 2021 edition of the Bloomberg Galaxy Crypto Index that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-50k-resistance-to-become-support-in-q4-bloomberg-commodity-strategist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $50,000 on Bitcoin}}}\uc2  may act as strong support during declines in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Could the recent rise in Bitcoin and altcoins attract profit-booking by traders or is this the start of a long-term uptrend? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin witnessed profit-booking on Oct. 7 but the bears could not pull the price below the breakout level at $52,920, which is a positive sign. The bulls tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-hits-56k-as-bulls-return-and-talk-focuses-on-bitcoin-etf-approval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resume the up-move today}}}\uc2  but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/3dff018e-053e-4419-8d21-b418ca8e1002.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The first support on the downside is $52,920 but if bears pull the price below this level, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the psychological level at $50,000 and then to the 20-day exponential moving average ($48,285).\par \par \uc2 The upsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) near the overbought zone indicate an advantage to buyers. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to resume the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above $56,100 could push the pair to $60,000 where bears may mount stiff resistance. This positive view will invalidate if the price plummets below the 50-day simple moving average ($47,342). The pair could then retest the critical 100-day SMA ($42,691) support.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) recovery rose above the immediate resistance at $3,676.28 today but the bulls may {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-risks-drop-below-3-2k-as-eth-price-faces-heavy-resistance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 find it difficult to sustain}}}\uc2  the price above it. The RSI is close to the downtrend line, which could act as a resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/93cbe881-c6c1-45df-8014-14709d5bd58d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level, the first support is at the 20-day EMA ($3,324). A strong rebound off this level will indicate that sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the likelihood of a rally to the stiff overhead resistance at $4,027.88. Conversely, if the price plummets below the 20-day EMA, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to the 100-day SMA ($2,899).\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to sustain Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above $433, suggesting that demand dries up at higher levels. The price has slipped back below $433 today and the bears will now try to pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($409).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5a35bf64-62ac-4cbd-b906-e3fd308d478f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the BNB/USDT pair could slide to the 100-day SMA ($379). Such a move could increase the possibility of the pair remaining range-bound between $320 and $450 for the next few days.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips. The bulls will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle at $450 and start the northward march toward $518.90.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 After several failed attempts in the past few days, the bulls managed to push and close Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($2.25) on Oct. 7. However, the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick showed that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/597ee41b-f968-48f4-b270-7760299ec4b2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price action of the past few days has formed a symmetrical triangle pattern, indicating that the bulls and bears are undecided about the next directional move. The 20-day EMA and the 50-day SMA ($2.47) are flat and the RSI is close to 50, indicating a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 This demand will tilt in favor of the bulls if the price turns up and breaks above the resistance line of the triangle. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rally to $2.47 where the bears may again mount a stiff resistance. A break above this level could open the doors for a rally to $2.80.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, a break below the support line of the triangle could pull the price down to the 100-day SMA ($1.96).\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  formed an inside-day candlestick pattern on Oct. 7, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears. The bulls tried to resolve the uncertainty to the upside today but could not clear the overhead hurdle at the 50-day SMA ($1.09).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/d9db351c-0147-4813-ae67-c683a43d2986.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The next directional move could start after bulls push the price above the 50-day SMA or bears sink the XRP/USDT pair below the 20-day EMA ($1.03). A break and close above the 50-day SMA could clear the path for a possible rally to $1.41.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, a break below the 20-day EMA could sink the price to the 100-day SMA ($0.92). The bulls have defended this support during the previous two retests and may again try to do that.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bears failed to sink Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) below the 20-day EMA ($153) for the past two days, indicating that bulls are defending the level vigorously. This may have attracted buying from the short-term bulls today, resulting in a strong rebound.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/6ee8c093-d2ac-4126-b2c7-4a78f176ed5c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers will now make one more attempt to push the price above the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80. If they can pull it off, the SOL/USDT pair could rally to $200 and then challenge the all-time high at $216.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the pair could slide to the 50-day SMA ($137). The bulls may attempt to defend this level but if they fail, the decline may extend to $116.\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the downtrend line on Oct. 6 but the bears have not been able to sink the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.23), indicating buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/8608889e-8300-4abc-b459-c2a16a2af9b8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has turned up and the RSI is in the positive zone, suggesting that bulls have the upper hand. If buyers propel the price above the downtrend line, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is likely to pick up.\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair could then rally to $0.32 and later to $0.35. Contrary to this assumption, if the price once again reverses direction from the downtrend line, the possibility of a break below the 20-day EMA increases. The pair may then drop to the $0.21 to $0.19 support zone.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/pro-crypto-senator-cynthia-lummis-discloses-up-to-100k-btc-purchase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-crypto senator Cynthia Lummis discloses up-to-$100K BTC purchase}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) broke above the resistance at $33.60 on Oct. 7 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests selling at higher levels. The inside-day candlestick pattern today signals indecision among bulls and bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/1303cad0-46a5-4820-9ad6-47f3379defee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI has reached the downtrend line which has been acting as a stiff resistance. If the price turns down from the current level, the bears will try to pull the DOT/USDT pair below the support at $28.60.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if bulls drive the price above $35.31, the pair could rise to $38.77. The bears may try to defend this level aggressively but if bulls overcome this resistance, the pair could rally to $42.60 and later to $49.78.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token recovered sharply and rose above the overhead resistance at $45.01 on Oct. 7 but the bulls could not clear the overhead hurdle at $49.54 today. This suggests that bears continue to defend the psychological level at $50.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/33e38a60-ae39-4ad3-bed4-fd3a1b8b203d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price has dipped back below $45.01 today and the bears will now try to pull the price down to the 20-day EMA ($39.63). This is an important support for the bulls because a strong rebound off it will suggest that sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 That will increase the possibility of a break above $50. If that happens, the LUNA/USDT pair could start the next leg of the uptrend toward $56.97 and then $65.97. On the contrary, a break below the 20-day EMA could result in a decline to the 50-day SMA ($34.92).\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ) seems to be forming the right shoulder of the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  inverse head and shoulders pattern, which will complete on a break and close above the neckline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c3b10542-26c8-4bf1-be25-e9abc9db99fc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Such a move could push the price to $31.41 and if this level is crossed, the rally could extend to the pattern target at $36.98. The 20-day EMA ($24.50) has started to turn up and the RSI is just above the midway, suggesting a minor advantage to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate if the UNI/USDT pair turns down from the current level and breaks below the critical support at $22. If that happens, the traders may rush to the exit, pulling the pair down to $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvNjRjZDM2MmEtOTVkOC00MzVhLWI1MDUtNjM2MTQ4MjdiMWYyLkpQRw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211008eha8000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/6: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , XRP, SOL, DOGE, DOT, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,841 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin lead a sharp recovery in the crypto sector on Wednesday with a strong up-move.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-returns-to-1t-asset-as-btc-price-blasts-to-55k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skyrocketed above the $1 trillion market capitalization }}}\uc2  on Oct. 6, pulling the total crypto market capitalization close to $2.3 trillion. This marks a complete 100% recovery from the June 22 lows when the total crypto market capitalization had plunged to about $1.15 trillion.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Chainalysis\uc2  , the Central and Southern Asia and Oceania region saw a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-transactions-surge-706-in-asia-as-institutional-adoption-grows-chainalysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 massive increase of 706% in crypto transactions }}}\uc2  between July 2020 and June 2021. The total transaction value was $572.5 billion, accounting for 14% of the global transaction value.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/3b0d41b9-6e64-40e1-b658-3c230aa041fb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360 }}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of America Corporation\uc2  (BoA) subsidiary, BofA Securities , published a report on Oct. 4 that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bank-of-america-offers-bullish-outlook-for-defi-and-nfts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 projected a \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  long-term picture for cryptocurrencies }}}\uc2 . The report estimated that by June 2021, about 221 million users will have traded cryptocurrencies or used a blockchain application, a massive increase from 66 million users in May 2020.\par \par \uc2 The BofA report said that the crypto sector was \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo large to ignore\u8221\'20\'1D and that it comprised \u8220\'20\'1Cso much more\u8221\'20\'1D than just Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Can Bitcoin pick up momentum and challenge the all-time high? Will this boost interest in altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke and closed above $48,843.20 on Oct. 4, which was the first sign that the correction might be over. This may have attracted short-covering by the bears, resulting in a rally on Oct. 5 and 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/07b88173-193e-474d-b771-de6f8c18dbee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls have thrust the price above $52,920, which invalidates the head and shoulders (H&S) pattern. The 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($46,947) has turned up and the relative strength index (RSI) is close to the overbought zone, indicating that bulls are in command.\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain a price above $52,920, the BTC/USDT pair could pick up momentum and rally to $60,000. This level may act as a resistance but if crossed, the pair could challenge the all-time high at $64,854.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price fails to sustain above $52,920, it will suggest that demand dries up at higher levels. The pair may then correct to $48,843.20.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH }}}\uc2  ) bounced off the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($3,317) on Oct. 4 and the bulls extended the recovery on Oct. 5. However, the bears tried to stall the rally on Oct. 6 and they pulled the price to the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/6164aa1c-052f-4fbf-a509-5c2d9c4ec38b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows aggressive buying near the 50-day SMA. The rising 20-day EMA ($3,262.50) and the RSI in the positive zone indicate that bulls are in control.\par \par \uc2 If buyers propel the price above $3,676.28, the ETH/USDT pair could rally to $4,027.88. The bears will have to pull and sustain the price below the 20-day EMA to open the gates for a possible decline to $3,000 and then to the 100-day SMA ($2,871).\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB }}}\uc2  ) broke and closed above the overhead resistance at $433 but the bulls have not been able to build on this strength. The bears pulled the price back below $433 on Oct. 6 but the positive sign is that bulls aggressively bought the dip as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/42b4ca9d-d871-436c-8067-709af3ee7e6e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($404) is sloping up and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating that buyers have the upper hand. If bulls push and sustain the price above $444, the BNB/USDT pair could rally to $518.90.\par \par \uc2 This level may again act as a stiff resistance but if bulls can overcome the hurdle, the momentum could pick up. Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the next stop could be the 100-day SMA ($377).\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have not been able to clear the overhead hurdle at the 20-day EMA ($2.25) in the past few days, indicating selling at higher levels. The long tail on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bulls are accumulating Cardano ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/06260759-418d-4f21-9a4f-f1cbc296aa87.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattening out and the RSI is just below the midpoint, suggesting a balance between supply and demand. If bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could rally to $2.47.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price once again turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears will try to sink the pair to $1.94. A break and close below this support could clear the path for a further decline to $1.60.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP }}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between the 20-day EMA ($1.02) and the 50-day SMA ($1.10) for the past few days. This shows that bulls are buying near the 20-day EMA while bears are defending the 50-day SMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5e68267a-02f0-436a-8206-9931b2b4fada.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn up and the RSI has climbed into the positive territory, indic