itical support at $116. If this level breaks down, the selling could intensify and the pair may plunge to the 100-day SMA ($84).\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE }}}\uc2  ) soared above the 20-day EMA ($0.22) on Oct. 4, indicating that bulls are attempting a comeback. The buyers pushed the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.25) on Oct. 5 but the bears successfully defended the downtrend line.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c98c78d3-d710-4258-ac6f-69463cb34b34.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Another attempt by the bulls to drive the price above the downtrend line is facing strong resistance today but the positive sign is that bulls are not giving up much ground. The 20-day EMA has turned up gradually and the RSI is in the positive zone, indicating that the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive and sustain the price above the downtrend line, the DOGE/USDT pair could rally to $0.32 and then to $0.35. Alternatively, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the pair could plummet to the $0.21 to $0.19 support zone.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bank-of-america-identifies-20-high-profile-us-companies-with-crypto-exposure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bank of America identifies 20 high profile US companies with crypto exposure }}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT }}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 50-day SMA ($30.21) on Oct. 4 but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels. The bears pulled the price back below the 50-day SMA today but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows aggressive buying near $28.60.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/a83f106f-51f4-441d-a434-e0935084cdb9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now try to propel the price above the overhead resistance at $33.60. If that happens, the DOT/USDT pair could rally to $38.77. This level may again act as a resistance but if the bulls can overcome the hurdle, the pair may start its journey toward $49.78.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level of $33.60, the bears will again try to pull the price below the neckline. Such a move will complete the H&S pattern, which has a target objective of $12.23.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token broke to a new all-time high on Oct. 4 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick showed profit-booking near the psychological level at $50. The token made an inside-day candlestick pattern on Oct. 5, indicating indecision among bulls and bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/510b27e0-55a3-4219-b754-45836b88984f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This uncertainty resolved to the downside today and the LUNA/USDT pair plunged to $40.38. However, lower levels attracted aggressive buying as seen from the long tail on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will now make one more attempt to push the price above $50 and resume the uptrend. On the other hand, the bears will try to stall the recovery and pull the price below the 20-day EMA ($38.57). If that happens, the pair may decline to the critical support at $32.50.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls are aggressively buying on dips to the 20-day EMA ($24.33) as seen from the long wick on the candlestick for the past two days. Today bears pulled Uniswap ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI }}}\uc2  ) below the 20-day EMA but bulls defended the 100-day SMA ($23.47).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e1ca0320-5594-477e-bd0a-d2cb973c936d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The gradually rising 20-day EMA and the RSI in the positive territory indicate a minor advantage to buyers. If bulls push and close the price above the neckline, the inverse H&S pattern will complete. This positive setup has a target objective of $36.98.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or from the neckline and breaks below $22, it will suggest that demand dries up at higher levels. The UNI/USDT pair could then drop to $18.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC }}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvMjJiYmNmZWEtZTYzMy00ZDk3LWFkZDMtMTk4ZWVhZTZjMzE3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211006eha6000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional bulls back Bitcoin after weeks of altcoin accumulation\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 406 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin investment products have posted inflows for three weeks in a row, with last week\u8217\'20\'19s total of $68.7 million marking a week-over-week increase of 36%.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors are pivoting back to digital gold with Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) investment products posting a third consecutive week of inflows.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 latest \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-49-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-927557c718c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , BTC investment products generated $68.7 million worth of inflows between Sept. 27 and Friday, representing a 36% increase in exposure week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 While products tracking BTC have now dominated inflows to \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products for two weeks in a row, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-investors-no-longer-fearful-watch-this-btc-price-level-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  turn}}}\uc2  comes fresh off a record streak of outflows that persisted for eight consecutive weeks until early September.\par \par \uc2 Total inflows for digital investment products were $90 million for the week, marking the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-investors-bought-the-dip-as-china-fud-broke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh consecutive week}}}\uc2  of inflows as institutional investors continue to increase exposure to digital assets.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors also snapped up a significant amount of Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) investment products, with inflows totaling $20.2 million. BTC and ETH products gained roughly 7.4% and 3.2% for the week, respectively.\par \par \uc2 There was also a mixed appetite for altcoins last week. Products tracking Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana (SOL) posting inflows of $1.1 million and $700,000, respectively, while Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT and Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) fund shed $800,000 each. Multi-asset funds also saw minimal inflows of $1.9 million.\par \par \uc2 Institutional demand for Solana appears to have bottomed out, with inflows to products tracking SOL crashing by 98% since posting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-exposure-to-altcoin-products-retests-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highs of $38.9 million}}}\uc2  five weeks.\par \par \uc2 Despite the markets recovering from July\u8217\'20\'19s violent pull-back, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  highlighted that last week\u8217\'20\'19s trade volume of $2.4 billion remains low compared to the $8.4 billion worth of institutional crypto products traded weekly during the height of 2021\u8217\'20\'19s bull cycle in mid-May.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/these-3-indicators-flashed-bullish-ahead-of-the-recent-bitcoin-price-pump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 These 3 indicators flashed \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  ahead of the recent Bitcoin price pump}}}\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 estimates, institutional asset managers currently represent combined assets under management (AUM) worth $57.1 billion combined \u8212\'20\'14 a weekly increase of 8.5%.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale continues to dominate the sector, representing $41.1 billion or 71% of the sector\u8217\'20\'19s total AUM. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  XBT and Purpose funds rank in second and third with $2.2 billion and $2.1 billion worth of AUM, respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZTJjOTU1OTktMDVhOC00NDc4LTg2YWQtZDEzYjllNjBhOTlmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211005eha50005s\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional bulls back Bitcoin after weeks of altcoin accumulation\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 406 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin investment products have posted inflows for three weeks in a row, with last week\u8217\'20\'19s total of $68.7 million marking a week-over-week increase of 36%.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors are pivoting back to digital gold with Bitcoin (BTC) investment products posting a third consecutive week of inflows.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 latest \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-49-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-927557c718c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , BTC investment products generated $68.7 million worth of inflows between Sept. 27 and Oct. 1, representing a 36% increase in exposure week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 While products tracking BTC have now dominated inflows to \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products for two weeks in a row, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-investors-no-longer-fearful-watch-this-btc-price-level-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  turn}}}\uc2  comes fresh off a record streak of outflows that persisted for eight consecutive weeks until early September.\par \par \uc2 Total inflows for digital investment products were $90 million for the week, marking the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-investors-bought-the-dip-as-china-fud-broke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh consecutive week}}}\uc2  of inflows as institutional investors continue to increase exposure to digital assets.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors also snapped up a significant amount of Ethereum (ETH) investment products, with inflows totaling $20.2 million. BTC and ETH products gained roughly 7.4% and 3.2% for the week respectively.\par \par \uc2 There was also a mixed appetite for altcoins last week. Products tracking Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), and Solana (SOL) posting inflows of $1.1 million and $700,000 respectively, while Polkadot (DOT) and Binance Coin (BNB) fund shed $800,000 each. Multi-asset funds also saw minimal inflows of $1.9 million.\par \par \uc2 Institutional demand for Solana appears to have bottomed out, with inflows to products tracking SOL crashing by 98% since posting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-exposure-to-altcoin-products-retests-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highs of $38.9 million}}}\uc2  five weeks.\par \par \uc2 Despite the markets recovering from July\u8217\'20\'19s violent pull-back, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  highlighted that last week\u8217\'20\'19s trade volume of $2.4 billion remains low compared to the $8.4 billion worth of institutional crypto products traded weekly during the height of 2021\u8217\'20\'19s bull cycle in mid-May.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/these-3-indicators-flashed-bullish-ahead-of-the-recent-bitcoin-price-pump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 These 3 indicators flashed \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  ahead of the recent Bitcoin price pump}}}\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 estimates, institutional asset managers currently represent combined assets under management (AUM) worth $57.1 billion combined \u8212\'20\'14 a weekly increase of 8.5%.\par \par \uc2 Grayscale continues to dominate the sector, representing $41.1 billion or 71% of the sector\u8217\'20\'19s total AUM. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  XBT and Purpose funds rank in second and third with $2.2 billion and $2.1 billion worth of AUM respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvZTJjOTU1OTktMDVhOC00NDc4LTg2YWQtZDEzYjllNjBhOTlmLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211005eha500005\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/4: BTC, ETH, BNB,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , SOL, XRP, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 2,012 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bulls have set their sights on $50,000 and this renewed push is also boosting large and small-cap altcoin prices.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is facing rejection near $50,000, indicating that bears are not ready to give up without a fight. Many analysts expect Bitcoin to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-bull-run-has-at-least-6-months-to-go-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soar in the last quarter of the year}}}\uc2  and stock-to-flow model creator PlanB says the \u8220\'20\'1Cworst-case scenario\u8221\'20\'1D for Bitcoin in October is $63,000 and $98,000 by November.\par \par \uc2 PlanB is not alone in his \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  projection. Using Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s relative strength index (RSI) indicator during the four-year cycle, Twitter commentator TechDev suggests that the second leg of the 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/200k-btc-price-programmed-as-bitcoin-heads-toward-2nd-rsi-peak"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bull run may just be getting started}}}\uc2 . The trader expects Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s cycle top to be around $200,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/8ccac884-a505-4eae-8483-8cd04a8425ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 While historical projections may be pointing for a rally in the last quarter, the rise may not be linear. The United States equity market\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October is 36% higher than the average for the remaining 11 months, according to CFRA chief investment strategist Sam Stovall. Due to Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s high correlation with the S&P 500, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bearish-pennant-breakdown-confirmed-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traders may be in for a roller coaster ride}}}\uc2  in October.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin follow its historical precedence and rally to the upside? And will altcoins join in on the party? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Bitcoin above the overhead resistance at $48,843.20 on Oct. 3 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates that bears are defending the level aggressively. The price has been trading between the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($46,667) and $48,843.20 for the past two days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/628cac71-536a-413a-8457-683e51b7c908.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive and sustain the price above the overhead resistance, the BTC/USDT pair could pick up momentum and rally to $50,000 and later to $52,920.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($45,478) has turned up and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating the path of least resistance is to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if bears pull the price below the 50-day SMA, the pair could drop to the 20-day EMA. A bounce off this support will be a positive sign and the bulls will make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle.\par \par \uc2 The advantage will tilt in favor of the bears if the price breaks and sustains below the 20-day EMA. The pair could then drop to the 100-day SMA ($41,935).\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line and the moving averages on Oct. 1, but the bears have not thrown in the towel yet. The sellers are attempting to stall the up-move near $3,500 and pull the price back below the 50-day SMA ($3,297).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/f83a0b29-848a-4a31-ac2e-ad0085d99fdc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, the ETH/USDT pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($3,194). This is an important support for the bulls to defend because a break below it could attract further selling. The pair may then drop to the psychological level at $3,000 and later to the 100-day SMA ($2,841).\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the moving averages, the bulls may make one more attempt to propel the price above $3,500. If the price sustains above this resistance, the pair could rise to $3,676.28 and then to $4,000.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been facing strong resistance at the overhead resistance at $433 but the positive sign is that bulls have not given up much ground. This indicates that buyers are holding on to their positions as they anticipate a move higher.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/16f35822-44b3-4032-a12c-acfeb3f106b3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($395) has turned up and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating a slight advantage to the bulls. If buyers drive and sustain the price above $433, the BNB/USDT pair could pick up momentum and rally to $518.90.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level, the pair may drop to the 20-day EMA. If the price rebounds off this level, the bulls will again try to push the pair above $433. A break and close below the 20-day EMA could keep the pair range-bound for a few days.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($2.25) for the past two consecutive days but they could not sustain the higher levels. This suggests that the sentiment remains negative and traders are defending the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/e780dbe3-5174-4ea6-9f31-f095b4077218.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down from the 20-day EMA on Oct. 4 and the bears will now try to sink the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair to the critical support at $1.94. If this level gives way, the pair could witness aggressive selling and plummet to $1.60.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off the $1.94 support and rises above the 20-day EMA. The pair could then rally to the 50-day SMA ($2.46) where bears may again mount a stiff resistance. A break above this level could clear the path for an up-move to $2.97.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana\u8217\'20\'19s (SOL) recovery reached the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $177.80 on Oct. 3. This level is acting as a stiff resistance and the bears are trying to pull the price to the 20-day EMA ($150).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/935276f3-0703-47ac-a866-cbe57f513efb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current levels or the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bulls are buying on dips. That will increase the possibility of a break above $177.80. If that happens, the SOL/USDT pair could rise to $200 and then retest the all-time high at $216.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that traders are closing their positions. The pair may then drop to the 50-day SMA ($129) and later to $116.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 RIpple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) rose above the 20-day EMA ($1.01) on Oct. 1 and bulls tried to push the price above the $1.07 overhead resistance on Oct. 3. However, the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears are defending the 50-day SMA ($1.10) forcefully.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/7696c092-7e22-4b6d-a4db-439707e72869.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price is currently stuck in the tight range between the 20-day EMA and the 50-day SMA. Both moving averages are flattish and the RSI is near the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 This balance will tilt in favor of buyers if the price breaks and sustains above the 50-day SMA. The XRP/USDT pair could then start its journey toward the next resistance at $1.41.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price breaks and sustains below the 20-day EMA, the pair could drop to the 100-day SMA ($0.90). A break below this support could signal that bears are back in command.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) broke above the moving averages and the downtrend line on Oct. 1, which was the first indication that bears may be losing their grip. The bulls tried to push the price above the right shoulder of the head and shoulders pattern on Oct. 2, but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/02111fcf-9f60-4fdd-8484-b65e87a3d651.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOT/USDT pair formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Oct. 3, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears. This uncertainty has resolved to the downside on Oct. 4 and the bears are trying to sink the price below the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, it will suggest that sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. The pair could then challenge the neckline of the H&S pattern.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the moving averages, the bulls will once again try to propel the price above the right shoulder and retest the critical resistance at $38.77.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/is-axie-infinity-overheating-axs-price-hits-record-high-following-100-qtd-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is Axie Infinity overheating? AXS price hits record high following 100% QTD rally}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  (DOGE) recovered to the 20-day EMA ($0.22) on Oct. 1, but the bulls have not been able to sustain the price above this resistance in the past few days. This shows that sentiment is negative and bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/70f7cb19-c88c-4d80-9ce2-9629da1ce16c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The long-legged Doji candlestick pattern on Oct. 4 shows that bulls are buying near the $0.21 support while bears are selling near the 100-day SMA ($0.24). If this uncertainty resolves to the downside, the DOGE/USDT pair could drop to $0.19 and then to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if bulls drive and sustain the price above the 100-day SMA, the pair could rally to the downtrend line, which could again act as a stiff resistance. A break and close above this level will be the first indication that the correction may be ending.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long wick on the Oct. 3 candlestick suggests that bears attempted to defend the $45.01 level but they could not sustain the lower levels. Aggressive buying by the bulls on Oct. 4 pushed Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token to a new all-time high.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/5b38b18b-547b-4b12-82de-fa8090930bf4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls sustain the price above $45.01, it will suggest the start of a new uptrend. The rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone indicate that bulls are in control. The LUNA/USDT pair could first rise to $50 and if this psychological hurdle is cleared, the next stop could be $65.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price fails to sustain above $45.01, the bears will try to pull the price down to the 20-day EMA ($37.45). A strong bounce off this support will suggest that the positive sentiment is intact. The bears will have to sink and sustain the price below the 50-day SMA ($33.56) to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) rose above the 50-day SMA ($25.46) on Oct. 2 but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears sold at higher levels. The altcoin formed an inside-day candlestick pattern on Oct. 3, indicating indecision among bulls and bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b5b9b89c-bfae-48a2-a7d5-7c39c72e402d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty resolved to the downside and bears pulled the price to the 20-day EMA ($24.02) on Oct. 4, but a positive sign is that bulls bought the dip aggressively, as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above $25, the bulls will again try to push the UNI/USDT pair above $27.62. Above this level, the pair could retest the critical resistance at $31.41.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if the price breaks below the moving averages, the pair could drop to $22. This is an important support for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the decline could extend to $18.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvYWZhYmUwNzEtMWE1NS00NzM4LThhZjItNmU4Y2I4N2Q0NjEyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211004eha4000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 10/1: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, LUNA, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,830 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Historical data suggests that October is a good month for Bitcoin bulls, and today\u8217\'20\'19s push above $47,600 could be a signal of what's to come for BTC and altcoins.\par \par \uc2 The month of September stayed true to its billing as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-history-repeating-3-indicators-suggest-october-will-reignite-the-btc-bull-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically weak period for cryptocurrencies}}}\uc2 . Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) closed the month with a loss of about 7%. However, October may bring cheer to the bulls because Bitcoin has risen in six of the past eight years, falling only in 2014 and 2018.\par \par \uc2 The bulls started the month on a positive note as bears scurried to close their short positions. Data shows that more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/say-hi-to-uptober-bitcoin-price-surges-above-47k-in-minutes-liquidating-270m-in-shorts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $270 million worth of short positions were liquidated}}}\uc2  within minutes. Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s enthusiasm was also shared by several altcoins which have surged higher today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/4398a9a4-cd40-4a87-920c-08b2698bb00f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has closely followed PlanB's Stock-to-Flow model projections in the past two months. If PlanB is lucky enough to be right for the third time, then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/analyst-nails-bitcoin-monthly-close-2-months-running-his-october-target-is-63k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin could rally to $63,000}}}\uc2 , which is the model's prediction for October.\par \par \uc2 Although the start to the month has been strong, will bulls be able to sustain the momentum and boost crypto prices further, or will higher levels attract selling by the bears?\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The repeated failure of the bears to sink Bitcoin below the 100-day simple moving average ($41,470) in the past few days could have attracted buying from aggressive bulls and short-covering from short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/29176253-adb9-4b7a-ab16-b0192f2835e6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum picked up on Oct. 1 after bulls pushed the price above the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($44,485). Sustained buying has driven the price above the 50-day SMA ($46,604).\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains above the 50-day SMA, the bulls will try to push the BTC/USDT pair above the right shoulder at $48,843.20. This could open the doors for an up-move to the stiff resistance at $52,920.\par \par \uc2 If the pair turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance but does not dip below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying on dips. The bears will have to pull the price back below the 20-day EMA to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) Sept. 29 candlestick shows that bears sold at higher levels but a positive sign is that bulls did not allow the price to break below the 100-day SMA ($2,794). This shows that bulls continued to accumulate at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b6dd83e9-bdf5-42d6-a0dd-6e28f1251744.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Aggressive buying in the past two days has pushed the price to the 50-day SMA ($3,290). The zone between the 50-day SMA and the downtrend line is critical for the bears to defend because if bulls push the price above it, the ETH/USDT pair could rise to $3,676.28.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index (RSI) has risen into the positive territory, suggesting that bulls are making a comeback. This view will be negated if the price turns down from the current level and plunges below the 100-day SMA.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) bounced off the $2.02 level on Sept. 29, indicating that bulls are attempting to defend the zone between the psychological level at $2 and $1.94. The recovery could face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA ($2.26).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/030b9b12-1348-42b5-af67-3c980e469e04.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies. The bears will then make one more attempt to sink the price below the 100-day SMA ($1.89).\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if bulls drive and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that demand exceeds supply. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($2.45), which is again likely to act as a stiff resistance. A break and close above this resistance could result in the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum picking up.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The sharp rally in Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) in the past two days suggests short-covering by the bears and buying by the aggressive bulls. The buyers have cleared the hurdle at the 20-day EMA ($384) and may now challenge the overhead resistance at $433.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c2c505a7-cfa7-4cd2-8802-646fc1c59b3c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from $433 but rebounds off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above $433 could clear the path for a possible rally to $518.90. The 20-day EMA has started to turn up and the RSI has jumped into the positive territory, indicating that bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to $340.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple's ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) tight range trading between the 20-day EMA ($0.99) and the 100-day SMA ($0.89) resolved to the upside on Oct. 1. The flattening 20-day EMA and the RSI near the midpoint suggest that bulls are back in the game.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/b6167d1e-a5ea-4360-87ec-6043aee76972.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the long wick on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that the bears have not yet given up and are trying to defend the 50-day SMA ($1.11). If the price turns down from the current level, the bears will try to pull the price to the 100-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, if bulls thrust and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA, it will suggest that the correction may be over. The XRP/USDT pair could then start its northward march toward the stiff resistance at $1.41.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Although bears successfully defended the 20-day EMA ($142) in the past few days, they could not pull Solana (SOL) below the support zone between the 50-day SMA ($122) and $116. This suggests that selling dried up at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/c247f529-19b0-4b67-ad22-ca14013c3234.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls have pushed the price above the 20-day EMA on Oct. 1, indicating that the corrective phase may be over. The SOL/USDT pair could now rise to the 50% Fibonacci retracement level at $166 and above it to the 61.8% retracement level at $177.80.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from either resistance but bounces off the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are viewing the dips as a buying opportunity. The bears will have to pull the price below $116 to gain the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls have pushed Polkadot (DOT) above the 20-day EMA ($30.11) and the downtrend line on Oct. 1, which is the first indication that the selling pressure may be reducing.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/bdce7c02-2904-4680-a992-19b57a1d5593.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattening 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest that bulls have a slight edge. If buyers sustain the price above the downtrend line, the DOT/USDT pair could rise to $33.60.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this resistance could attract aggressive buying and the pair may rally to $38.77. Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the neckline, the pair could enter a downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-nfts-can-be-a-riskier-investment-than-cryptocurrencies-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why NFTs can be a riskier investment than cryptocurrencies, report}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) tight range trading between $0.19 and $0.21 resolved to the upside on Oct. 1, indicating that bulls have absorbed the selling. The bulls will next try to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.22), which could act as a stiff resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/0bf2eccb-0c5c-4612-996f-e5b506e78f7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA but does not slip below $0.21, it will suggest that traders are buying on dips. That will increase the likelihood of a break above the 20-day EMA. If that happens, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA and slips below $0.21 it will suggest that demand dries up at higher levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up on a close below $0.19.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token broke below the 20-day EMA ($35.02) on Sept. 28 but the bears could not capitalize on this breakdown. The bulls purchased at lower levels and pushed the price back above the 20-day EMA on Sept. 30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/55c92808-c8af-4490-8d3f-962dd54d5c54.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LUNA/USDT pair is currently facing stiff resistance at the downtrend line but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bulls are accumulating on dips. This increases the possibility of a break above the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 If the price closes above the downtrend line, it will suggest that the correction may be over. The pair could then retest the all-time high at $45.01. This \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will be invalidated if the price turns down from the current level and plummets below the 50-day SMA ($32).\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls repeatedly failed to sustain Uniswap\u8217\'20\'19s (UNI) price above the downtrend line of the descending channel in the past few days but the positive sign is that they did not give up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-10/4cc4ddf7-168b-45af-92ed-c20981573e9f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Strong buying on Oct. 1 has propelled the price above the channel and to the overhead resistance at the 50-day SMA ($25.72). This is an important level for the bears to defend because if this resistance cracks, the UNI/USDT pair could pick up momentum.\par \par \uc2 The pair could then rise to $27.62, followed by a rally to the critical resistance at $31.41. Conversely, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA, the bears will make one more attempt to sink the pair below $22.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMTAvOTZiNDMwODktOWE5YS00ZmRhLTg3NmUtMDA2MWJkMmM0ZmNjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020211001eha1000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/29: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,861 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A week-long pattern of daily lower highs suggests bulls will be unable to flip $43,000 to support and this could weigh on the fledgling recovery seen across many altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) are attempting to bounce off their critical support levels as bulls try to thwart attempts by the bears to deepen the correction.\par \par \uc2 Tesla CEO Elon Musk said at the Code Conference in California recently that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-is-impossible-to-destroy-says-tesla-ceo-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 governments cannot \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroy crypto,\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  due to its decentralized nature but can \u8220\'20\'1Cslow down its advancement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Data shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-whales-move-record-btc-value-as-metric-sounds-alarm-over-price-volatility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whales have been moving record amounts}}}\uc2  of Bitcoin in the past two weeks. The total transfer volume of transactions worth $10 million and higher have surpassed levels seen when Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price was near $60,000.\par \par \uc2 According to on-chain analytics resource Material Indicators, \u8220\'20\'1Csmaller\u8221\'20\'1D whales sold and mega whales added to their holdings.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/9b6e81b5-1927-451b-b312-11a69ee2c145.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Bobby Lee, the former CEO of BTCC exchange, said in an interview with Bloomberg on Sept. 29 that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-fomo-rally-long-overdue-that-could-see-btc-price-top-200k-bobby-lee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s rally is expected to begin in 2021}}}\uc2 , which will not only push the price to an all-time high but also clear the psychological mark at $100,000 and possibly reach $200,000.\par \par \uc2 Are Bitcoin and altcoins getting ready for a relief rally or will bears pull the price below the respective support levels? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin continues to trade between the 100-day simple moving average ($41,221) and the 20-day exponential moving average ($44,229). The price has rebounded off the 100-day SMA today, indicating that bulls continue to defend this support aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/89755f69-f4cc-4d53-99c5-5efa7131e138.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is sloping down and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the negative zone, indicating that the sentiment remains negative and bears may sell on rallies. If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the tight range action may continue for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 A break and close below the 100-day SMA could result in panic selling and pull the price down to $37,332.70. If this level also cracks, the BTC/USDT pair could plummet to $30,000.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, a break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the selling pressure could be reducing. The pair may then rise to the 50-day SMA ($46,580), followed by a move to $48,843.20.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether turned down from the 20-day EMA ($3,118) on Sept. 27 and dropped to the 100-day SMA ($2,771) on Sept. 28. The bulls have once again held the support and are attempting to push the price toward the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b0a17492-317f-451a-a396-de95a28042d8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative territory suggest that bears remain in control. If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA, the bears will make one more attempt to break the 100-day SMA support.\par \par \uc2 If that happens, the ETH/USDT pair could slide to $2,400 and if this support also gives way, the decline could extend to $1,972.12. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above $3,174.50 to signal that the correction may be over. The pair could then rise to the 50-day SMA ($3,291) and then to $3,676.28.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been trading between the 20-day EMA ($2.27) and the $1.94 support for the past few days. The long wick on today\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears are selling on relief rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ec89a3a1-8885-4275-95ea-4b1d51f8ca0c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI below 40 indicate that bears have the upper hand. The sellers may make one more attempt to sink and sustain the price below the zone between $1.94 and the 100-day SMA ($1.87).\par \par \uc2 If the price slips below this support zone, the selling could pick up momentum and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could decline to $1.60 and later to $1.40. This negative view will invalidate if bulls drive and sustain the price above $2.47.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) closed below the $340 support on Sept. 27 but the bears could not capitalize on this move and sink the price below $320. This shows that selling dries up at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/f21f2d8f-af2d-40ad-8539-c918d2c015fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI has formed a positive divergence, indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be weakening. The strong rally today indicates aggressive buying at lower levels and possible short-covering by the bears.\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA ($381), it will suggest that the correction may be over. The BNB/USDT pair could then rally to $433.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price again turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that traders are selling on rallies. The bears will then make one more attempt to pull the price below $320.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  again dropped to the 100-day SMA ($0.88) on Sept. 28. Repeated retests of a support level tend to weaken it but a minor positive sign is that the bulls have successfully defended the level on several occasions in the past few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/3c4caad4-9425-4aca-b2fe-3a125e4bda99.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed the price to the 20-day EMA ($1.00) today but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears are in no mood to relent.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level, the bears will make one more attempt to sink and sustain the price below the 100-day SMA. If they succeed, the XRP/USDT pair could decline to $0.69.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if bulls drive the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair could rally to the 50-day SMA ($1.11).\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Although Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has broken out of the downtrend line, the bulls are struggling to sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($141). This suggests that sentiment remains negative and bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/332d990d-964e-466f-a5d9-7aee3349aa4b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first indication that the selling pressure could be reducing. The SOL/USDT pair may then rise to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level at $154.20 and then to the 50% retracement level at $166.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA or the overhead resistance, the bears will try to pull the pair below the 50-day SMA ($118). A break and close below $116 could result in panic selling.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) is attempting to rebound off the neckline of the developing head and shoulders pattern. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/48fd9042-0a62-4bed-bd8a-8644990f34ca.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling could pick up momentum below the neckline, pulling the price to the 100-day SMA ($22.28) and then toward the pattern target at $12.23. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($30.12) and the RSI just below the midpoint suggest a slight advantage to bears.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls thrust the price above the 20-day EMA and the downtrend line, it will indicate that bears may be losing their grip. The pair could then rally to $33.60 where bears may again pose a stiff challenge. A break and close above this resistance could clear the path for a retest at $38.77.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/vortecs-report-this-key-trading-algo-spotted-bullish-altcoin-setups-even-as-btc-price-fell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 VORTECS\u8482\'21\'22 Report: This key trading algo spotted \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  altcoin setups even as BTC price fell}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) is sandwiched between $0.19 and $0.21 for the past three days. This tight-range trading suggests indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ff5f69a4-14cd-4c1b-87e0-eaf83a17606b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RSI is attempting to form a positive divergence, suggesting that the selling pressure could be reducing. If bulls thrust the price above $0.21, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to the 20-day EMA ($0.22) which could again act as a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first indication of strength and could open the gates for a possible up-move to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below $0.19, the pair could plummet to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Avalanche\u8217\'20\'19s (AVAX) Sept. 27 candlestick shows that bears aggressively sold on rallies. The selling continued and bears pulled the price below the support line of the ascending channel on Sept. 28.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/64d04bc3-10e4-4711-ac7e-abb33b9b4dc8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although bulls have pushed the price back into the channel today, the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bears are selling on every minor recovery. The 20-day EMA ($62.12) has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, indicating that bulls may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 If the price fails to sustain inside the channel, the AVAX/USDT pair could slide to the next support at $52. Conversely, if bulls sustain the price inside the channel, the pair may rise to $72 and if this level is crossed, a retest of the all-time high at $79.80 is possible.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Uniswap ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/uniswap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UNI}}}\uc2  ) above the downtrend line of the descending channel in the past two days but they could not sustain the higher levels. However, a minor positive is that bulls have not given up much ground and are again trying to scale the overhead resistance today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b784977e-aeef-4759-9a79-c355a004f7c1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA ($23) and the RSI near the midpoint suggest that bears are losing their grip. If the price sustains above the channel, the UNI/USDT pair could rise to the 50-day SMA ($25.88) and later to $27.62.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above $27.62 may result in a retest of the stiff overhead hurdle at $31.41. Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level, it will suggest that bears are aggressively defending the resistance. If the pair slips below $21.84, the next stop could be $17.73.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvYWU1YzlhN2QtNWYzZi00NjdhLWFkMmQtYTdhNWM2ZTM2Nzk1LkpQRw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210929eh9t000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional investors bought the dip as China FUD broke\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 407 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Institutional investors snapped up $50.2 million worth of Bitcoin investment products last week, marking a 234% increase week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors were buying the dip on the back of China\u8217\'20\'19s latest FUD, with \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products generating $95 million worth of inflows last week.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Monday \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-48-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-6e597facca0f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2 , a surge in dip buying helped drive a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-investors-increase-their-crypto-holdings-for-5th-straight-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sixth consecutive week of inflows}}}\uc2  for institutional crypto investment products broadly.\par \par \uc2 The $95 million worth of inflows between Sept. 20 and Friday marks a 126% weekly inflows increase. Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) investment products led the pack with $50.2 million and $28.9 million worth of inflows, respectively.\par \par \uc2 While BTC investment products have seen outflows in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-traders-flock-to-solana-as-demand-for-eth-and-btc-flattens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 of the past 17 weeks}}}\uc2 , positive sentiment toward the asset rose during September as inflows were recorded for the past three weeks. Inflows to Bitcoin products also increased by 234% week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 Institutional appetites for altcoins appear to remain strong, with products tracking Solana (SOL), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT posting inflows of $3.9 million, $2.6 million and $2.4 million, respectively. Multi-asset funds also saw inflows of $6.4 million this past week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-has-recovered-from-china-s-fud-nearly-two-dozen-times-in-the-last-12-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto has recovered from China's FUD over a dozen times in the last 12 years}}}\par \par \uc2 The great wall of FUD\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \uc2 People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2  (PBoC) published a memo announcing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/all-bark-and-some-bite-china-s-bitcoin-ban-puts-traders-in-the-fear-zone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on all crypto transactions}}}\uc2  that triggered an 8% dip in the price of Bitcoin along with a wider pullback across the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 The PBoC\u8217\'20\'19s updated measures \u8212\'20\'14 which were initially published on Sept. 3 before it was picked up by western media outlets last week \u8212\'20\'14 outlined that financial institutions and payment firms are barred from providing any services related to crypto transactions.\par \par \uc2 While FUD from Chinese regulators has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically impacted crypto markets}}}\uc2 , it has also served as a catalyst for surging prices or bull runs in the subsequent months following the announcements.\par \par \uc2 In September 2017, China\u8217\'20\'19s government banned crypto exchanges from offering services to users in the country while also barring citizens from participating in initial coin offerings. Following the double ban, the price of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC made the historic climb}}}\uc2  from the $4,000 range to a then all-time high price of around $20,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvMzZmNmRkZjktZTFhYy00ZTQ1LWJjZmUtZDRjMGVmNTQ5NTQ0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210928eh9s0005w\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 CoinShares\par \b \uc2 Institutional investors bought the dip as China FUD broke\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 409 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Institutional investors snapped up $50.2 million worth of Bitcoin investment products last week, marking a 234% increase week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 Institutional investors were buying the dip on the back of China\u8217\'20\'19s latest FUD, with \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products generating $95 million worth of inflows last week.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Sept. 27 \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Weekly report, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/volume-48-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-6e597facca0f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surge}}}\uc2  in dip buying helped drive a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-investors-increase-their-crypto-holdings-for-5th-straight-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sixth consecutive week of inflows}}}\uc2  for institutional crypto investment products broadly.\par \par \uc2 The $95 million worth of inflows between Sept. 20 and Sept. 24 marks a 126% weekly inflows increase. BTC and Ether investment products led the pack with $50.2 million and $28.9 million worth of inflows respectively.\par \par \uc2 While BTC investment products have seen outflows in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-traders-flock-to-solana-as-demand-for-eth-and-btc-flattens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 of the past 17 weeks}}}\uc2 , positive sentiment towards the asset rose during September as inflows were recorded for the past three weeks. Inflows to Bitcoin products also increased by 234% week-over-week.\par \par \uc2 Institutional appetites for altcoins appears to remain strong, with products tracking Solana (SOL), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and Polkadot (DOT) posting inflows of $3.9 million, $2.6 million and $2.4 million respectively. Multi-asset funds also saw inflows of $6.4 million this past week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-has-recovered-from-china-s-fud-nearly-two-dozen-times-in-the-last-12-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto has recovered from China's FUD over a dozen times in the last 12 years}}}\par \par \uc2 The great wall of FUD\par \par \uc2 On Sept. 24 the \uc2 People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2  (PBoC) published a memo announcing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/all-bark-and-some-bite-china-s-bitcoin-ban-puts-traders-in-the-fear-zone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on all crypto transactions}}}\uc2  that triggered an 8% dip in the price of Bitcoin (BTC) along with a wider pullback across the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 The PBOC\u8217\'20\'19s updated measures \u8212\'20\'14 which were initially published on Sept. 3 before it was picked up by western media outlets last week \u8212\'20\'14 outlined that financial institutions and payment firms are barred from providing any services related to crypto transactions.\par \par \uc2 While FUD from Chinese regulators has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically impacted crypto markets}}}\uc2 , it has also served as a catalyst for surging prices or bull runs in the subsequent months following the announcements.\par \par \uc2 In September of 2017, China\u8217\'20\'19s government banned crypto exchanges from offering services to users in the country, while also barring citizens from participating in initial coin offers. Following the double-ban, the price of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC made the historic climb}}}\uc2  from the $4,000 range to a then all-time high price of around $20,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvMzZmNmRkZjktZTFhYy00ZTQ1LWJjZmUtZDRjMGVmNTQ5NTQ0LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210928eh9s00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/27: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, LUNA\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,888 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and most major altcoins have recovered from last week\u8217\'20\'19s sell-off, but they are still facing selling at higher levels, suggesting that the market could remain range-bound for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) recovered a large part of the losses that happened due to the knee-jerk reaction to China's regulatory crackdown on Sept. 24. This suggests that crypto markets have absorbed the news-based selling, with long-term investors likely using the dip to accumulate.\par \par \uc2 However, a rally may have to wait as market participants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-house-of-reps-to-deliver-verdict-on-infrastructure-bill-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watch the outcome of the infrastructure bill}}}\uc2  this week, which could see the debate start on Sept. 27 and the final vote on Sept. 30. The broad definition of a \u8220\'20\'1Cbroker\u8221\'20\'1D may cause some \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in crypto markets but HODLers are unlikely to be shaken.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/19c2f080-a3dc-43f0-92bb-b9dacbe700e4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Analyst Willy Woo said that \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin has entered the Never Gonna Give You Up phase of the Astley Cycle,\u8221\'20\'1D which could be followed by a rally.\par \par \uc2 On one side are the \u8220\'20\'1CRick Astley\u8221\'20\'1D investors and on the other end of the spectrum is JPMorgan CEO Jamie Dimon who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/jpmorgan-ceo-says-bitcoin-price-could-rise-10x-but-still-won-t-buy-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains steadfast in his criticism of Bitcoin}}}\uc2 . In an interview with Times of India, Dimon said that he won\u8217\'20\'19t buy Bitcoin even if it rises \u8220\'20\'1C10 times in price in the next five years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin extend its recovery in the next few days or is a range-bound action likely? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been oscillating between the 100-day simple moving average ($41,078) and the 20-day exponential moving average ($44,982) for the past few days, indicating that bulls are buying on dips while bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/17cbd383-6c41-4c94-8c08-9c54cd92c5a7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) just below the midpoint suggest that the path of least resistance is to the downside. If bears sink and sustain the price below the 100-day SMA, the selling could intensify.\par \par \uc2 The BTC/USDT pair could then drop to $37,332.70 and if this level also gives way, the decline may extend to $30,000.\par \par \uc2 This \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  view will invalidate if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages. Such a move will suggest that the bulls are back in the game. The pair could then rally to $48,843.20 and later to $52,920.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on Ether\u8217\'20\'19s candlesticks of the past three days shows that bulls are aggressively buying near the 100-day SMA ($2,756). Hence, this becomes an important level to watch out for.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/1a9d6009-d49c-411c-aa06-055ec5598105.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($3,193) is sloping down and the RSI is just below the midpoint, indicating that bears have a slight edge. If the price turns down from the current level, the ETH/USDT pair could consolidate between the moving averages for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 A break and close below the 100-day SMA could intensify selling and the pair may drop to $2,400 followed by a drop to $1,972.12. On the other hand, a break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign of strength. The pair could then rise to $3,600.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) above the moving averages on Sept. 25 but they could not clear the hurdle at $2.47. This suggests that bears have not given up and are selling on rallies to overhead resistance levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/61f705dd-0cd5-4995-b5ea-09a3d664a8e2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair has turned down and the bears will now try to sink the price to the critical support at $1.94. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because if it cracks, the pair could start a downtrend.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off $1.94, the bulls will again try to propel the pair above $2.47. If they manage to do that, it will indicate that the correction could be over. The pair could then rally to $2.97.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the support at $340 on Sept. 26 but the bulls bought the dip and held the level on a closing basis. The buyers are currently struggling to sustain the price above $340, indicating selling on minor rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/08245dd4-f1f5-4765-a00b-efd316136a0d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down and breaks below the $340 to $320 support zone, the BNB/USDT pair could extend the decline to $300 and later to $250. The 20-day EMA ($388) is sloping down and the RSI is below 37, suggesting that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA. Such a move will suggest that the selling pressure is reducing. The pair could then rally to the overhead resistance at $433.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  has repeatedly bounced off the 100-day SMA ($0.88) in the past few days, indicating that bulls are aggressively defending the support. The bulls will now try to push the price above the overhead resistance zone between the 20-day EMA ($1.02) and the 50-day SMA ($1.10).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/063a8f4c-6045-45b0-a593-4bc8b23c35be.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they manage to do that, it will suggest that the correction could be over. The XRP/USDT pair could then rise to $1.41 where bears may again mount a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone indicate that bears are in control. If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the pair could drop to the 100-day SMA. If this level holds, the pair may remain stuck between the moving averages for a few days.\par \par \uc2 The next leg of the down move could begin if bears sink and sustain the price below the 100-day SMA. That could clear the path for a possible drop to $0.69.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) broke out of the downtrend line and the 20-day EMA ($143) today, which suggests that the bears may be losing their grip. The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is just above the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/4f2411a9-0616-4b48-a87a-c0d3c6da7d12.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The short-term advantage could tilt in favor of the bulls if they push and sustain the price above $152.50. The SOL/USDT pair could then rally to $171.47 where the bears may again mount a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance, the bears will try to pull the price down to the 50-day SMA ($114). A break and close below this support could suggest a change in trend. On the other hand, a break and close above $171.47 could push the pair to $200.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 50-day SMA ($28.76) on Sept. 26 but the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick suggests that bulls are attempting to defend the neckline of the head and shoulders pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/8905c123-1ad2-4442-86d5-ab92a38ea839.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers attempted to push the price above the overhead resistance at the 20-day EMA ($30.91) today but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick indicates that bears are selling on rallies.\par \par \uc2 If bears pull the DOT/USDT pair below the 50-day SMA, a retest of the neckline is possible. A break and close below this support will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  H&S pattern, which has a pattern target at $12.23.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if bulls drive the price above the downtrend line, the pair could rise to $33.60 and later to $38.77.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/2021/09/27/before-nfts-surging-interest-pre-cryptopunk-collectibles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Before NFTs: Surging interest in pre-CryptoPunk collectibles}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) plummeted and closed below the $0.21 support on Sept. 24. Sustained selling pulled the price to $0.19 on Sept. 26 but the positive sign is that bulls defended this level aggressively as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/371f0a95-2c26-40b3-85c8-5b31da2531a2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to push the price above the overhead resistance at $0.21. If they succeed, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to the 20-day EMA ($0.23), which is likely to act as a stiff resistance.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears may pull the pair to $0.19. A break and close below this support could sink the pair to $0.15. Conversely, a break and close above the 20-day EMA could result in an up-move to the 50-day SMA ($0.26).\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on Avalanche\u8217\'20\'19s (AVAX) Sept. 26 candlestick suggests strong demand at lower levels. The bulls will now try to push the price to the all-time high at $79.80.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/0f21640c-87ee-47e6-a690-420436784806.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A breakout and close above the all-time high will signal the resumption of the uptrend. The bears may attempt to stall the up-move at the resistance line of the channel but if bulls overcome this hurdle, the AVAX/USDT pair could pick up momentum and rally to $100.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the support line of the channel, the pair could start a deeper correction. A break below the breakout level at $60.04 could open the gates for a decline to the 50-day SMA ($46.23).\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token turned down from $41.28 on Sept. 24 but the positive sign is that bulls did not allow the price to break below the 20-day EMA ($34.51). This suggests that bears are selling on rallies and bulls are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/98dc1aca-e37b-4f3f-ac8c-224071e85ab9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The indicators are giving conflicting signals with the upsloping moving averages indicating advantage to buyers while the negative divergence on the RSI warns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 If bulls drive the price above the downtrend line, the LUNA/USDT pair could retest the all-time high at $45.01. A break and close above this resistance will suggest the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level or the downtrend line and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the decline could extend to the 50-day SMA ($30.43).\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvNjNkZDgyMjktYWQyYi00OGE2LWIzN2YtYjYzNDBiNzA4ZmFjLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210927eh9r000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ether\par \b \uc2 Ethereum price gets back to $3K as institutional investors pile into ETH futures\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 611 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ethereum prices recovered on Sunday amid a market-wide upside correction but received an additional upside boost from a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  JPMorgan & Chase report.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s native token, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), staged a rebound on Sept. 26 following a massive decline earlier this week that saw its prices plunging to as low as $2,651 on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USD exchange rate rose 3.63% to hit an intraday high of $3,030. The upside move amounted to a 14.3% upside retracement from the pair\u8217\'20\'19s week-to-date low at $2,651, showing that traders attempted to retain their \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  bias despite potential headwinds ahead.\par \par \uc2 Last week, ETH prices fell due to a flurry of issues arising from China. On Monday, traders dumped crypto assets en masse after a tumult in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-crash-was-it-actually-evergrande-watch-the-market-report-live-w-eric-crown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s heavily indebted property market}}}\uc2  prompted a sell-off across global stock markets.\par \par \uc2 A rebound move ensued later in the week but met with another sell-off on Friday after the \uc2 People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/all-bark-and-some-bite-china-s-bitcoin-ban-puts-traders-in-the-fear-zone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reiterated that crypto transactions are illegal}}}\uc2 . Nonetheless, Ether bulls maintained their foothold and pushed prices back above $3,000, a psychological resistance level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/6dd7760f-f690-4b6a-a147-38c91ce12aa6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sentiments were similar across some top crypto assets, with the benchmark cryptocurrency, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), hitting an intraday high of $43,767 on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  following a 2.49% upside move. Meanwhile, Uniswap\u8217\'20\'19s native asset, UNI, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uniswap-uni-price-jumps-by-15-in-defi-cryptocurrency-market-rebound"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also fared higher}}}\uc2  by more than 19%, becoming the top-performing crypto asset in the previous 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Ether\u8217\'20\'19s top rivals Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana (SOL) performed poorly, with \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD dropping more than 5% and SOL/USD {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/derivatives-data-suggests-solana-has-reached-a-short-term-top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing over 3%}}}\uc2  on a 24-hour adjusted timeframe.\par \par \uc2 Institutional demand\par \par \uc2 Ether gains also followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/big-investors-pivoting-from-bitcoin-to-ether-futures-jpmorgan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  report}}}\uc2  from \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 . The study noted that institutional investors have started increasing their exposure in Ether markets.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  credited the ongoing craze in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/altcoin-roundup-there-s-more-to-defi-than-just-providing-liquidity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized finance}}}\uc2  (DeFi) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-gaming-a-catalyst-to-mainstream-adoption-of-decentralized-finance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nonfungible token}}}\uc2  (NFT) sector as the primary driver behind investors\u8217\'20\'19 interest in Ether. They added that the 21-day average Ethereum Futures premium climbed to 1% over spot ETH prices, citing the Chicago Mercantile Exchange data recorded since August.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b3055f38-33db-4ef8-857a-588912056af9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum Futures daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  report coincided with a record amount of Ether tokens getting withdrawn out of all crypto exchanges, as per data provided by CryptoQuant. At press time, the net ETH reserves on trading platforms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptoquant.com/overview/eth-exchange-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had dropped to 18.44 million ETH}}}\uc2  compared to 23.94 million ETH a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-drops-more-than-bitcoin-as-china-escalates-crypto-ban-eth-btc-at-3-week-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum drops more than Bitcoin as China escalates \b  \highlight22crypto ban\b0 \highlight22 , ETH/BTC at 3-week low}}}\par \par \uc2 Independent analyst PostyXBT also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostyXBT/status/1442048590034075663"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anticipates}}}\uc2  a potential further price rebound in Ether markets, noting that the cryptocurrency\u8217\'20\'19s latest declines had pushed it inside a classic accumulation range, as shown in the chart below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/0595328e-a775-4cea-9577-a7cd0714e514.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD weekly price chart featuring its latest accumulation range. Source: PostyXBT, TradingView\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWeekly close equally as important for ETH today as price tests the previous range highs as support,\u8221\'20\'1D the analyst noted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeems like a logical area to make a higher low and I have bought more here for long-term bags/swing trade. RR looks favorable after a 33% correction from the local top.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvYWQyYmU0ODEtZjJkMi00NDVjLThiOTQtM2JmOTZkMDIxOTYyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210927eh9q0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ether\par \b \uc2 Ethereum price gets back to $3K as institutional investors pile into ETH futures\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ethereum prices recovered on Sunday amid a market-wide upside correction but received an additional upside boost from a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  JPMorgan & Chase report.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum's native token Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) staged a rebound on Sept. 26 following a massive decline earlier this week that saw its prices plunging to as low as $2,651 on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USD exchange rate rose 3.63% to hit an intraday high of $3,030. The upside move amounted to a 14.3% upside retracement from the pair's week-to-date low at $2,651, showing that traders attempted to retain their \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  bias despite potential headwinds ahead.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Ether prices fell due to a flurry of issues arising from China. On Monday, traders dumped crypto assets en masse after a tumult in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-crash-was-it-actually-evergrande-watch-the-market-report-live-w-eric-crown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China's heavily indebted property market}}}\uc2  prompted a selloff across global stock markets.\par \par \uc2 A rebound move ensued later in the week but met with another selloff on Friday after \uc2 People's Bank of China{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/all-bark-and-some-bite-china-s-bitcoin-ban-puts-traders-in-the-fear-zone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reiterated that crypto transactions are illegal}}}\uc2 . Nonetheless, Ethereum bulls maintained their foothold and pushed prices back above $3,000, a psychological resistance level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/6dd7760f-f690-4b6a-a147-38c91ce12aa6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView.com\par \par \uc2 The sentiments were similar across some top crypto assets, with the benchmark cryptocurrency Bitcoin hitting an intraday high of $43,767 on \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  following a 2.49% upside move. Meanwhile, Uniswap exchange's native asset UNI {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uniswap-uni-price-jumps-by-15-in-defi-cryptocurrency-market-rebound"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also fared higher}}}\uc2  by more than 19%, becoming the top-performing crypto asset at least in the previous 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Ethereum's top rivals Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/derivatives-data-suggests-solana-has-reached-a-short-term-top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) performed poorly, with \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD dropping more than 5% and SOL/USD losing over 3% on a 24-hour adjusted timeframe.\par \par \uc2 Institutional demand\par \par \uc2 Ethereum gains also followed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/big-investors-pivoting-from-bitcoin-to-ether-futures-jpmorgan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a \b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  report}}}\uc2  thifrom JPMorgan & Chase. The study noted that institutional investors have started increasing their exposure in Ethereum markets.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  credited the ongoing craze in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/altcoin-roundup-there-s-more-to-defi-than-just-providing-liquidity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized finance}}}\uc2  (DeFi) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-gaming-a-catalyst-to-mainstream-adoption-of-decentralized-finance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nonfungible token}}}\uc2  (NFT) sector as the primary driver behind investors' interest in Ethereum. They added that the 21-day average Ethereum Futures premium climbed to 1% over spot ETH prices, citing the Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) data recorded since August.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b3055f38-33db-4ef8-857a-588912056af9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum Futures daily price chart. Source: TradingView.com\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  report coincided with a record amount of Ether tokens getting withdrawn out of all crypto exchanges, as per data provided by CryptoQuant. At press time, the net ETH reserves on trading platforms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptoquant.com/overview/eth-exchange-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had dropped to 18.44 million ETH}}}\uc2  compared to 23.94 million ETH a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-drops-more-than-bitcoin-as-china-escalates-crypto-ban-eth-btc-at-3-week-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum drops more than Bitcoin as China escalates \b  \highlight22crypto ban\b0 \highlight22 , ETH/BTC at 3-week low}}}\par \par \uc2 Independent analyst PostyXBT also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostyXBT/status/1442048590034075663"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anticipates}}}\uc2  a potential further price rebound in Ethereum markets, noting that the cryptocurrency's latest declines had pushed it inside a classic accumulation range, as shown in the chart below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/0595328e-a775-4cea-9577-a7cd0714e514.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD weekly price chart featuring its latest accumulation range. Source: PostXBT, TradingView.com\par \par \uc2 "Weekly close equally as important for ETH today as price tests the previous range highs as support," the analyst noted.\par \par \uc2 "Seems like a logical area to make a higher low and I have bought more here for long-term bags/swing trade. RR looks favorable after a 33% correction from the local top."\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvYWQyYmU0ODEtZjJkMi00NDVjLThiOTQtM2JmOTZkMDIxOTYyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210926eh9q0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin  \highlight22\uc2 volatility \highlight\uc2  continues as BTC price closes in on critical weekly close\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 496 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price swings up and down post-China "ban" ahead of Bitcoin weekly close.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) briefly fell below $42,000 on Saturday, Sept. 25, as the weekend looked set to deliver an unimpressive weekly close.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/cabf6fa8-107e-4ed9-94fe-7444051cfe18.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Trader: Bitcoin \u8220\'20\'1Cfine\u8221\'20\'1D above $38,000\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD losing $1,000 in just over an hour during Saturday before rebounding.\par \par \uc2 The weekend had started with the pair at around $43,000 \u8212\'20\'14 a critical level {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bounces-again-after-briefly-losing-40k-support-watch-these-btc-price-levels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some say}}}\uc2  should hold as the weekly close looms.\par \par \uc2 Others argue that lower price action would also be suitable for Bitcoin in the aftermath of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with $36,000\u8211\'20\'13$38,000 as the cut-off point for bulls.\par \par \uc2 Among them is Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe critical level for Bitcoin is still the same, which is between $38-40K I\u8217\'20\'19d prefer to see the level hold,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441477544277073923"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers late Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that happens, everything is fine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among commentators, the China \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D story still dominated the debate, this roping in the industry\u8217\'20\'19s best-known names after a kneejerk reaction from nervous traders sent cryptocurrencies tumbling.\par \par \uc2 Despite the chaos, nothing from China had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/old-fud-new-btc-price-dip-month-old-china-crypto-ban-sparks-42k-bitcoin-price-drop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 really changed}}}\uc2 , with the government repeating its existing position. As Cointelegraph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2 , when the \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D initially began in September 2017, Bitcoin conversely saw a new all-time high just three months later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing has created more wealth in the past decade than technologies banned in China,\u8221\'20\'1D Michael Saylor, CEO of MicroStrategy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michael_saylor/status/1441389129665818626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BTC Price change 60d pre and post prior China "ban" events {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uyGTxB9iuJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uyGTxB9iuJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Geenty (@geenty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/geenty/status/1441403448562388994?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Jon Geenty, a data scientist at analytics firm Coin Metrics, meanwhile, produced a comparative chart showing how Bitcoin performs after each China \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D story. Contrary to fears, BTC price action has in fact {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-has-recovered-from-china-s-fud-nearly-two-dozen-times-in-the-last-12-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stabilized after such events}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Crypto market cap lines up broad support retest\par \par \uc2 The outlook for altcoins remained bleak on the day, thanks to Bitcoin doubling down on lower levels.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-9-24-btc-eth-ada-bnb-xrp-sol-dot-doge-avax-luna"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/24: BTC, ETH, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, LUNA}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) stood at around $2,825, near the essential $2,800 support level for bulls, while most of the top 10 cryptocurrencies by market capitalization lost 6%\u8211\'20\'137% on the day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/613902db-6244-4427-8c2d-045b784c81df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAltcoin market capitalization also on crucial level here,\u8221\'20\'1D van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2 , adding that the total crypto market cap could still see a \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful retest\u8221\'20\'1D of support on its weekly close. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072/photo/1}}}\par \par \uc2 Total market capitalization for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}\uc2  making a beautiful retest here?\par \par \uc2 Depending on the weekly, but crucial level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JcK1zDo22m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JcK1zDo22m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe (@CryptoMichNL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441564356769054731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 25, 2021}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvZWI3NjA5ZTEtNWI3ZC00NjljLWE1NmQtN2FkZjU2M2E2ODEyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210927eh9p0008k\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin  \highlight22\uc2 volatility \highlight\uc2  continues as BTC price closes in on critical weekly close\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By William Suberg \par \uc2 493 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 BTC price swings up and down post-China "ban" ahead of Bitcoin weekly close.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) briefly fell below $42,000 on Sept. 25 as the weekend looked set to deliver an unimpressive weekly close.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/cabf6fa8-107e-4ed9-94fe-7444051cfe18.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Trader: Bitcoin "fine" above $38,000\par \par \uc2 Data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pro.cointelegraph.com/?via=markets&_ga=2.121254216.1571181373.1628517932-1136475544.1627545224"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraph Markets Pro}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\uc2  showed BTC/USD losing $1,000 in just over an hour during Saturday before rebounding.\par \par \uc2 The weekend had started with the pair at around $43,000 \u8212\'20\'14 a critical level {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bounces-again-after-briefly-losing-40k-support-watch-these-btc-price-levels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some say}}}\uc2  should hold as the weekly close looms.\par \par \uc2 Others argue that lower price action would also be suitable for Bitcoin in the aftermath of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with $36,000-$38,000 the cut-off point for bulls.\par \par \uc2 Among them is Cointelegraph contributor Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe.\par \par \uc2 "The critical level for Bitcoin is still the same, which is between $38-40K I'd prefer to see the level hold," he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441477544277073923"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers late Friday.\par \par \uc2 "If that happens, everything is fine."\par \par \uc2 Among commentators, the China "ban" story still dominated the debate, this roping in the industry's best-known names after a kneejerk reaction from nervous traders sent cryptocurrencies tumbling.\par \par \uc2 Despite the chaos, nothing from China had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/old-fud-new-btc-price-dip-month-old-china-crypto-ban-sparks-42k-bitcoin-price-drop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 really changed}}}\uc2 , with the government repeating its existing position. As Cointelegraph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2 , when the "ban" initially began in September 2017, Bitcoin conversely saw a new all-time high just three months later.\par \par \uc2 "Nothing has created more wealth in the past decade than technologies banned in China," Michael Saylor, CEO of MicroStrategy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/michael_saylor/status/1441389129665818626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BTC Price change 60d pre and post prior China "ban" events {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uyGTxB9iuJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uyGTxB9iuJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Geenty (@geenty) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/geenty/status/1441403448562388994?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Jon Geenty, a data scientist at analytics firm CoinMetrics, meanwhile produced a comparative chart showing how Bitcoin performs after each China "ban" story. Contrary to fears, BTC price action has in fact {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-has-recovered-from-china-s-fud-nearly-two-dozen-times-in-the-last-12-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stabilized after such events}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Crypto market cap lines up broad support retest\par \par \uc2 The outlook for altcoins remained bleak on the day, thanks to Bitcoin doubling down on lower levels.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/price-analysis-9-24-btc-eth-ada-bnb-xrp-sol-dot-doge-avax-luna"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 9/24: BTC, ETH, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, LUNA}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) stood at around $2,825, near the essential $2,800 support level for bulls, while most of the top ten cryptocurrencies by market cap lost 6-7% on the day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/613902db-6244-4427-8c2d-045b784c81df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD 1-hour candle chart (\uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 ). Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 "Altcoin market capitalization also on crucial level here," Van de Poppe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2 , adding that the total crypto market cap could still see a "beautiful retest" of support on its weekly close. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441602105144451072/photo/1}}}\par \par \uc2 Total market capitalization for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Crypto?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Crypto}}}\uc2  making a beautiful retest here?\par \par \uc2 Depending on the weekly, but crucial level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JcK1zDo22m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JcK1zDo22m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe (@CryptoMichNL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoMichNL/status/1441564356769054731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 25, 2021}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvZWI3NjA5ZTEtNWI3ZC00NjljLWE1NmQtN2FkZjU2M2E2ODEyLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210925eh9p0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/24: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, LUNA\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,778 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins made a sharp downside move to their recent lows after news that China banned crypto trading surfaced.\par \par \uc2 The crypto market\u8217\'20\'19s recovery was rocked on Sept. 24 after news that China's government is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/chinese-regulators-unite-forces-to-crack-down-on-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adopting a new set of measures}}}\uc2  that includes stronger inter-departmental coordination to \u8220\'20\'1Ccut off payment channels, dispose of relevant websites and mobile applications\u8221\'20\'1D to crack down on illegal cryptocurrency transactions efficiently.\par \par \uc2 Although the news has caused a selloff, long-term investors are unlikely to be perturbed because, apart from announcing additional measures to enforce the existing ban effectively, there is nothing else that has changed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/2560adfa-a6bf-4b02-a42f-11e7807b22af.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 China first announced a ban on cryptocurrencies back in September 2017 and that news had also resulted in a sharp correction in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price. However, that dip proved to be a good buying opportunity because the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sound-familiar-september-2017-china-bitcoin-ban-sparked-20k-all-time-high-in-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 price recovered within a few weeks}}}\uc2  and went on to hit a new all-time high close to $20,000 in less than three months.\par \par \uc2 Is the current correction in Bitcoin and most major altcoins a good buying opportunity or could the crypto markets tumble further? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top-10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bounced off the 100-day simple moving average ($40,874) and rose above the neckline of the head and shoulders pattern on Sept. 22. That showed strong demand at lower levels but the recovery could not clear the hurdle at the 20-day exponential moving average ($45,596).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e4771b3e-d236-4b5a-951e-c7d25c813056.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) in the negative zone indicate that bears have the upper hand. If bears sink and sustain the price below the 100-day SMA, the BTC/USDT pair could decline to $37,332.70.\par \par \uc2 This level may act as a strong support but if it cracks, the next stop could be at the pattern target at $32,423.05.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns up from the current level or the 100-day SMA, the bulls will again try to drive the pair above the moving averages. A close above the 50-day SMA ($46,816) will suggest that the correction may be over.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the 100-day SMA ($2,734) on Sept. 22 and rose above the breakdown level at $3,000. This shows that bulls bought the dip and tried to trap the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b3d141fc-8583-4302-ad68-b77dd5b80f7e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the recovery stalled at $3,174.50 on Sept. 23 and the bears are attempting to establish their supremacy. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($3,255) and the RSI below 41 indicate that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 If the index breaks and closes below the 100-day SMA, the ETH/USDT pair could witness aggressive selling. The pair could then drop towards the pattern target at $1,972.12. This negative view will invalidate if bulls drive and sustain the price above the moving averages.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/cardano"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) strong rebound off the $1.94 level hit a roadblock at the 20-day EMA ($2.36). This suggests that sentiment remains negative and traders are selling on rallies to the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/3104f784-d931-4e9f-aeb8-bc1bb9659442.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will now try to sink the price below the critical support zone at $1.94 and the 100-day SMA ($1.83). If they succeed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could plummet to $1.60 and then to $1.40.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rises from the current level or rebounds off $1.94, the bulls will again attempt to clear the overhead hurdle. A break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the correction may be over. The pair could then rally to $2.60 and then $2.80.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) rebound off the strong support at $340 turned down from $385.30 today, indicating strong selling by traders at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/05db9434-2a1c-4a85-9c21-22a60cae157b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($402) and the RSI below 37 indicate that bears are in control. If the $340 support cracks, the selling could intensify and the BNB/USDT pair could extend its decline to $300 and then to $250.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will make one more attempt to push the price above the moving averages. A break and close above $433 will signal that the correction may have ended.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/ripple"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  bounced off the 100-day SMA ($0.87) on Sept. 22 but the bulls could not extend the recovery. The altcoin formed a Doji candlestick pattern on Sept. 23, indicating indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/290e246f-fe44-49db-9586-5b27692b79ab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty resolved to the downside today as bears have pulled the price down to the 100-day SMA. If this support gives way, the selling could pick up momentum and the XRP/USDT pair could slide to $0. 70.\par \par \uc2 This level may act as a strong support but if bears sink the price below it, the next stop could be $0.50. This negative view will be negated if the price rebounds off the 100-day SMA and rises above the $1.07 to $1.13 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/solana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) bounced and rose above the 20-day EMA ($145) on Sept. 22 but the bulls could not push the price above the downtrend line. This suggests that bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/1577a62c-fe2a-40ca-b25c-d427cbb00242.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears have pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA today and the SOL/USDT pair could now drop to the 50-day SMA ($108). This level is likely to act as a strong support.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off it, the bulls will again try to thrust and sustain the price above the downtrend line. If they can pull it off, the pair could rise to $170 and then to $200.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the 50-day SMA cracks, the pair could witness panic selling and the price could then drop to the 78.6% Fibonacci retracement level at $98.26.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/polkadot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) rebound off $25.50 stalled at $33.60. This suggests that bears are selling at higher levels. The bears are attempting to pull the price below the breakout level at $28.60. If they manage to do that, a retest of $25.50 is likely.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/874a26d9-d8f2-4cb1-bd27-2e84ae8f3915.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A break and close below $25.50 will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. The DOT/USDT pair could then start its decline to the 100-day SMA ($21.87) and then to the pattern target at $12.23.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the current level or the neckline, the bulls will make one more attempt to resume the up-move. A break and close above $33.60 could open the doors for a retest at $38.77.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-hits-45k-twtr-stock-price-rises-3-8-after-btc-tipping-comes-to-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin hits $45K, TWTR stock price rises 3.8% after BTC tipping comes to Twitter}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tags/dogecoin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above $0.21 on Sept. 22 but the recovery failed to attract buyers at higher levels. After forming an inside-day candlestick pattern on Sept. 23, the price has dropped below $0.21 today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/a219450d-f74b-411c-ad64-80aeef6a6fb7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.23) and the RSI near 36 suggest that sellers have the upper hand. If bears sink the price below the $0.19 support, the DOGE/USDT pair could extend its decline to the critical support at $0.15.\par \par \uc2 This level has held on three previous occasions, hence the bulls will again try to defend it. On the other hand, if bears sink the price below $0.15, the selling may intensify and the pair could plummet to $0.10.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche (AVAX) rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($60.15) on Sept. 21 and rose to a new all-time high on Sept. 23. However, the bulls could not thrust the price above the resistance line of the ascending channel, which may have resulted in profit-booking by short-term traders.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/aa4c12b7-5a8c-4782-801b-00ade02f2b59.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The AVAX/USDT pair has turned down today and the first stop could be the support line of the channel. A strong rebound off this support will indicate that the uptrend remains intact and traders are accumulating on dips. The pair could then rise to $94.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a break and close below the channel will be the first sign that the bulls may be losing their grip. If bears pull the price below the 20-day EMA, the pair could plummet to $48 and then to the 50-day SMA ($43.06).\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls successfully defended the retest of the breakout level in Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token on Sept. 21. This suggested that sentiment remained positive and traders viewed the dips as a buying opportunity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/a06706f9-7850-4fef-bcba-a8f7ff8eb0a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers pushed the price above the 20-day EMA ($33.06) on Sept. 22 and followed that up with another up-move on Sept. 23. Although the 20-day EMA has started to turn up, the RSI is showing a negative divergence, indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may be weakening.\par \par \uc2 If bears pull and sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, the LUNA/USDT pair could again drop to the critical support at $22.40. This is an important level to watch out for because if it cracks, the selling could intensify and the pair may drop to $18.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, if bulls drive the price above $40, the pair could retest the all-time high at $45.01. A breakout and close above this level could signal the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvM2U1MjdiY2QtYTU2OS00NjVkLWExMTUtMTYzOGNjYjUxYTIxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210924eh9o000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Diminishing returns: Is Bitcoin underperforming compared to altcoins?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nikolai Kuznetsov \par \uc2 1,378 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 SOL, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ETH have all had epic runs recently, but are they leaving BTC in the dust?\par \par \uc2 The first half of 2021 in the crypto markets brought many comparisons to 2017. Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) was on a tear to its all-time high, the new frontier of decentralized finance emerged, and nonfungible tokens were gaining myriad celebrity endorsements.\par \par \uc2 But after the initial months of euphoria and a subsequent sell-off, BTC\u8217\'20\'19s performance has been far more lackluster. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/extreme-fear-as-bitcoin-falls-below-40k-then-recovers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent market sell-off}}}\uc2  resulting from the Evergrande crisis has compounded fears. However, it can\u8217\'20\'19t be ignored that many altcoins, particularly platform tokens, have undergone impressive runs and, in some cases, even bucked broader market trends.\par \par \uc2 With hopes still high that another bull run is likely during this halving cycle, should BTC holders be worried that the flagship asset is underperforming?\par \par \uc2 2021 by the numbers\par \par \uc2 Between January and reaching its all-time high (ATH) of nearly $65,000 in April, BTC posted gains of 113%. Based on current prices, the year-to-date (YTD) gains are around 45%.\par \par \uc2 By comparison, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) gained 497% between January and its ATH in May, while its year-to-date rose over 300% despite taking a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-s-spot-setup-looks-grim-but-derivatives-data-tells-a-different-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent battering}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, even ETH\u8217\'20\'19s impressive gains are nothing compared to rival platform tokens. Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has posted a staggering YTD increase above 1,000% while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/200-smart-contracts-launch-on-cardano-but-there-s-a-catch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 barely yet supporting}}}\uc2  any real activity. Solana\u8217\'20\'19s SOL has even dwarfed that figure by rising over 8,000% since January. This comes after dropping from its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-rally-mimicking-ethereum-why-a-500-sol-price-target-could-be-conservative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all-time high above $200}}}\uc2 . Honorable mentions go to Polygon (MATIC), Avalanche (AVAX) and Terra (LUNA), all of which have undergone impressive rallies in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Gregory, CEO of Currency.com, told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGenerally, there is a lot of enthusiasm for Web 3.0, whether that\u8217\'20\'19s powering the metaverse with ETH, or much faster transaction times with SOL, or whatever the future holds for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 . People see holding layer-one protocols as strong value picks for the future. Investing in sound tech and following the momentum and progression of the asset class following real-world use cases seems to be prudent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Why are altcoins outperforming BTC?\par \par \uc2 On the face of it, the numbers do indeed seem to indicate that BTC is underperforming compared to other coins. One factor that could explain this is the law of diminishing returns. BTC is the oldest asset and twice the age of Ether. Although Bitcoin has delivered eye-popping returns during its lifetime \u8212\'20\'14 making billionaires out of early adopters \u8212\'20\'14 is it possible that the flagship asset can continue to deliver three- or four-figure returns as it ages? Given that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s entire economic model is based around the principle of diminishing returns, with block rewards halving every four years or so, it seems plausible.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, as Cointelegraph has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/joining-the-ranks-bitcoin-s-correlation-with-gold-and-stocks-is-growing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2 , as more investors and institutions pile in, Bitcoin has begun to mirror other assets. We can note this effect in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.buybitcoinworldwide.com/volatility-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dampening}}}\uc2  of Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  over time.\par \par \uc2 Arguably, the only reason that markets continue to grow is that investors continually seek out new assets of value. Therefore, while BTC appears to be delivering lower returns, it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t surprise anyone that investors are interested in more volatile assets to profit from price movements.\par \par \uc2 But that leads to other questions: Is there a risk of creating a self-fulfilling negative cycle from BTC? As investors look to other assets to earn large gains, will BTC inevitably become less attractive?\par \par \uc2 Or, if we dare to imagine it, does the current appetite for platform tokens indicate that investors\u8217\'20\'19 sentiment toward Bitcoin is gravitating to the \u8220\'20\'1Cno intrinsic value\u8221\'20\'1D argument? After all, stronger fundamentals and potential for adoption is perhaps the one big selling point that platform tokens have over Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Micha Benoliel, co-founder and CEO of decentralized Internet-of-Things network Nodle, believes that platform tokens have a bright future ahead, but perhaps not at the expense of BTC. He told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the market is just beginning to understand the value of blockchain ecosystems and services. That\u8217\'20\'19s why altcoins are performing so well. Bitcoin, which is more a store of value, is on its trajectory and is becoming a crypto asset class with less risk and for people with a long-term investment strategy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Is $100,000 Bitcoin still realistic?\par \par \uc2 From another angle, even if Bitcoin returns are diminishing compared to their historical highs, gains continue to outstrip other assets, such as stocks and gold, by far. At the current rate of diminishment, BTC will continue to deliver superior performance for quite some time to come. As such, it seems unlikely that an exodus is imminent. Daniele Bernardi, CEO of investing firm Diaman Group, told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course, Bitcoin appears to be underperforming compared to small- and medium-cap coins in percentage terms. But don\u8217\'20\'19t forget the large difference in capitalization. If BTC prices increase by 10%, it would raise the market cap by $80 billion. If Solana, for example, increases by 100%, the real value in market cap goes up by $40 billion. For this reason, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s any basis for doubting Bitcoin or its position as the market-leading asset.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As far as the bull trajectory goes, it\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that in 2017, Bitcoin gained 1,900% between January and December. However, until now in 2021, it\u8217\'20\'19s only up around 450%. If prices do follow the same pattern, that will put us on track for a year-end BTC price of around $138,000.\par \par \uc2 That estimate is eerily close to the $135,000 year-end price predicted by the stock-to-flow (S2F) model, which continues to be the most accurate forecast of Bitcoin prices. Indeed, August\u8217\'20\'19s BTC closing price is, give or take, exactly as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/100trillionUSD/status/1406577006230245376?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  by S2F creator PlanB back in June, and September\u8217\'20\'19s could be on track to follow suit.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin stands firm\par \par \uc2 The numbers illustrate that BTC\u8217\'20\'19s returns are indeed diminishing over time across consecutive bull cycles. But this shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be surprising to anyone, considering Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s economic model. Micha\u235\'00\'EBl van de Poppe, Cointelegraph contributor and full-time trader, agrees, telling Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInvestors shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be worried. It\u8217\'20\'19s actually a natural habit of the markets to slow down and have lengthening cycles. This is something we will see more often in the future and will actually open up the gates for more investors. The less Bitcoin will be swinging around with their performance and daily movements, the better as an asset in your portfolio.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, gradually decreasing returns should not detract from the fact that Bitcoin is, by any measure, delivering a healthy performance in line with even the most \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts. According to Igneus Terrenus, head of communications at Bybit, BTC is still by far the go-to coin for newcomers \u8212\'20\'14 institutions or individuals \u8212\'20\'14 entering the space. He told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin remains the best investment-grade crypto asset for institutional investors. And a relatively more stable ranging pattern may actually help Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s case as an alternative to gold and add fuel to its long-term rise. When one zooms out to five years or 10 years \u8212\'20\'14 horizons familiar to whales and institutional investors \u8212\'20\'14 Bitcoin returns beat everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also impossible to say whether any of the recent platform token rallies would have happened if BTC had been languishing in long-term bear territory, as money {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dominance-cycle-suggests-the-2017-crypto-rally-could-repeat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tends to flow}}}\uc2  down from BTC.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more, the models show that there\u8217\'20\'19s still every reason to believe in a year-end BTC price above six figures. Currency.com\u8217\'20\'19s Gregory agreed despite the increasing demand for platform tokens. He told Cointelegraph, \u8220\'20\'1CBTC is outperforming the market but is currently being held back by macro market trends and events on Wall Street. However, historically, Q4 has been the strongest for BTC, and it is likely history repeats itself before the end of 2021.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, while BTC is in no danger of losing its status as crypto\u8217\'20\'19s flagship asset, soaring altcoins undeniably offer bigger opportunities right now for those who believe they can time the markets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvZDNkYzQzYTktNzY4Mi00Nzc0LWI3YWYtZjM0NDNhNjJhYjA5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210924eh9o000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Strong buying at lower levels has resulted in a sharp recovery in Bitcoin and altcoins today.\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/22: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, AVAX, UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,815 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Positive news about China\u8217\'20\'19s Evergrande meltdown and the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s intent to continue its current monetary policy catalyzed a strong recovery in the price of Bitcoin and altcoins.\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets and United States equity markets are attempting recovery on Sept. 22 as fears of a widespread contagion due to Chinese developer Evergrande defaulting on its debt recede. \uc2 Bridgewater Associates\uc2  co-chairman and co-chief investment office \uc2 Ray Dalio\uc2  said on Sept. 22 that Evergrande\u8217\'20\'19s debt was \u8220\'20\'1Cmanageable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ming Tan, a director at the credit rating agency \uc2 Standard & Poor\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/evergrande-buy-the-dip-or-bail-pundits-weigh-in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese government may step in and restructure Evergrande}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Crypto Fear & Greed Index had plunged to 21 levels, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fear-greed-index-suggests-bitcoin-s-price-is-undervalued"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicating extreme fear}}}\uc2  among investors. However, while speaking on CNBC, Galaxy Digital CEO Mike Novogratz said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-in-good-shape-as-long-as-btc-price-stays-above-40k-mike-novogratz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto markets remain in good shape}}}\uc2  as long as Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) sustains above $40,000 and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) stays above $2,800.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/4443f313-49e6-4ee7-abcb-3e4daeb7c2f2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Traders may now shift their focus to the Federal Reserve\u8217\'20\'19s policy statement with economic and interest rate forecasts on Sept. 22, which will be followed by a press conference by Fed Chair Jerome Powell.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin and altcoins sustain the rebound or will higher levels attract selling by the bears? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin plunged below the neckline on Sept. 21, which completed the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. However, a positive was that the bulls have pushed the price back above the neckline on Sept. 22. This suggests strong buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/f34f8be3-69dc-4cd6-9d8d-5afbfcaa40fe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers sustain the price above the neckline, it could trap several aggressive bears, resulting in a short squeeze. The BTC/USDT pair could then rally to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($46,038) where bears may pose a stiff challenge.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index (RSI) is in the negative zone, indicating that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 If the price fails to sustain above the neckline, the bears will attempt to resume the downtrend. The first support on the downside is $37,332.70 and then the pattern target at $32,423.05.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the moving averages will be the first indication that the correction may be over.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether plummeted and closed below $3,000 on Sept. 20, which completed the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. Usually, the breakdown from the neckline is retested and that is what happened on Sept. 22.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/a98b9c08-c036-4dc4-a0fa-e9585af883e6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative zone, indicating advantage to bears. If the price turns down from the current level, the bears will attempt to resume the down move toward the pattern target at $1,972.12.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if bulls sustain a price above $3,000, it will indicate an accumulation on dips. The ETH/USDT pair could then rally to the 20-day EMA ($3,303), which may again act as a stiff resistance. A breakout and close above this level could signal that bulls are back in the game.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is in a strong corrective phase but the bulls are attempting to arrest the decline at the strong support at $1.94, where they are likely to run into a wall at the 20-day EMA ($2.38).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ee2c4a42-3f2b-4ca4-93b9-2a9c48e8a017.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are close to completing a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative territory, suggesting that bears have the upper hand. If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears may again challenge the $1.94 support.\par \par \uc2 A break and close below this level could open the doors for a further fall to $1.60. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA to indicate the start of a sustained recovery. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then rise to $2.60 and later to $2.80.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke below the Sept. 7 low at $369 on Sept. 20 and reached strong support at $340 on Sept. 21. The bulls are currently attempting to defend this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/dde85b53-5603-44fb-ae8a-15f7bd924f3b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is below 41, indicating that bears are at an advantage. Any pullback is likely to be met with strong selling near the 20-day EMA ($410).\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below $340, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the psychological support at $300 and then to $250. This negative view will be negated if bulls propel and sustain the price above the overhead resistance at $433.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) plunged and closed below the Sept. 7 intraday low at $0.95 on Sept. 20, suggesting that supply exceeds demand. The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative zone, indicating that bears have the upper hand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/908f2c23-1f4a-4a52-bc7a-68b7cd895c30.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The current relief rally is likely to hit a hurdle at the 20-day EMA ($1.06). If the price turns down from this resistance, it will indicate that traders continue to sell on rallies. The bears will then attempt to resume the down move.\par \par \uc2 If the price slips below $0.85, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to the next support at $0.75. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the overhead resistance zone at $1.07 to $1.13 to indicate strength.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) broke and closed below the 20-day EMA ($144) on Sept. 20, which is the first sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may be weakening. The bulls attempted to push the price back above the 20-day EMA on Sept. 21 but failed, indicating that bears are attempting a comeback.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/bd4127d7-c406-45a0-ae86-c63c47548ae7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The SOL/USDT pair rebounded off the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $123.42 and has reached the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA and the downtrend line, the pair could rise to $171.47. This level may again act as a resistance but a break above it could result in a move to $200 and then to $216.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level or the downtrend line, it will suggest selling at higher levels. The bears will then try to sink the price below $123.42 and extend the decline to the 50-day simple moving average ($104).\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) broke below the 50-day SMA ($27.71) on Sept. 21 but bulls bought the dip aggressively and reclaimed the level on Sept. 22. That seems to have trapped the bears, resulting in a short squeeze.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/7d734ce2-7fdc-4c92-b0c2-ba590acd3d1c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOT/USDT pair has reached the 20-day EMA ($31.42) which is an important level to watch out for. If buyers drive the price above this resistance, the pair could rise to $35 and then retest $38.77.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that traders are selling on rallies. The bears will then make one more attempt to pull the price to the Sept. 7 intraday low at $22.66.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-bounces-again-after-briefly-losing-40k-support-watch-these-btc-price-levels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin bounces again after briefly losing $40K support \u8212\'20\'14 Watch these BTC price levels}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) broke and closed below the $0.21 support on Sept. 20, but the bears could not crack the next support at $0.19. This suggests demand at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/20e41147-8dee-4b85-8745-a1107ad64298.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to sustain the price above $0.21 on Sept. 22. If that happens, the DOGE/USDT pair could rise to the 20-day EMA ($0.24). The bears are likely to defend this level aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, the bears will make one more attempt to sink the price below the $0.21 to $0.19 support zone. If they manage to do that, the pair could drop to the critical support at $0.15.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the downtrend line to indicate that the correction could be over.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 Avalanche (AVAX) bounced back sharply from the 20-day EMA ($56.34) on Sept. 22, suggesting that the sentiment remains positive and traders are buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/2acaa43d-19ac-43ef-93a4-d02a33b94349.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers have pushed the price above the overhead resistance at $66.24, increasing the possibility of a retest of the all-time high at $76.27. A breakout and close above this resistance will signal the resumption of the uptrend.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance, it will indicate that higher levels are attracting profit-booking. The bears will then make one more attempt to sink the price below the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the AVAX/USDT pair could start a deeper correction to $48 and then to the 50-day SMA ($40.49).\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) broke and closed below the Sept. 7 intraday low at $21, suggesting that traders are rushing to the exit. The price is presently correcting inside a descending channel pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/3f038b8d-5e1c-47b9-b0f7-077edbb27745.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($24.10) is sloping down and the RSI is below 41, indicating that bears have the upper hand. Any rebound from the current level is likely to face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this resistance, the UNI/USDT pair could drop to the support line of the channel. A break below $18 could open the doors for a possible decline to $13.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate if the price breaks and closes above the descending channel. The pair could then gradually move up to $27.62.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvYTM3NzQ1YzItODhlNy00ZjNiLTkzODMtYzAwMTQwZjRjNjFlLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210922eh9m000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 DeFi\u8217\'20\'19s potential means more institutional demand for next-gen tokens\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Shiraz Jagati \par \uc2 1,482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Institutions are only just getting their toes wet when it comes to DeFi, and therefore, the next few months could be extremely interesting in terms of how they become further involved.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no denying that the last couple of years have seen the altcoin sector blossom and have a major impact on the crypto market at large. In fact, a quick look at data available on Google Trends shows us that searches related to the term \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum killer\u8221\'20\'1D have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=today%203-m&geo=IN&q=ethereum%20killer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soaring}}}\uc2  over the past 90-days, signaling a growing interest among investors in various altcoins.\par \par \uc2 In this regard, a few cryptocurrencies \u8212\'20\'14 such as Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana (SOL), Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT and Terra (LUNA) \u8212\'20\'14 have made a major market push recently. SOL, in particular, has been turning a lot of heads among investors, thanks in large part to its most recent rally, which saw the cryptocurrency surge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-sharp-fall-from-50k-linked-to-stronger-us-dollar-gold-correlation-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite the market experiencing a massive selloff}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, there are several other networks that have shown a lot of promise. For example, following the completion of its much-hyped Alonzo hard fork, Cardano, too, has been able to record substantial profits, posting numbers of +70% and +1,200% over the last 90 and 180 days, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Demand for next-generation tokens soars\par \par \uc2 To gain a better idea of what the aforementioned developments mean for the market at large, Cointelegraph reached out to Antoni Trenchev, managing partner and co-founder of lending platform Nexo. In his view, there is growing institutional demand for coins such as Solana\u8217\'20\'19s SOL and Terra\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA, something that is made evident by the fact that both assets have been able to make their way into the list of top 15 cryptocurrencies by total market capitalization. Trenchev told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a reflection of companies going deeper into crypto. Over the first two months of 2021, major institutions like BlackRock, Square and \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  were only just dipping their toes into Bitcoin. Now they\u8217\'20\'19ve tasted its benefits and are looking to harness the untapped potential of up-and-coming blockchains and DeFi coins that could yield higher returns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trenchev highlighted that such developments suggest that the crypto market may currently be in the midst of an alt-season; however, what\u8217\'20\'19s different this time around is that established coins such as ETH and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) are showing a higher level of stability in comparison to some of these newer assets. \u8220\'20\'1CThink of the current situation as alt season meets institutional interest, and yes, I think we will see more and more trends like this in the future,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The stability these institutions bring became fairly evident on Sept. 16 when Solana experienced a major outage wherein instead of going into a panic-induced sell frenzy, SOL barely lost any of its value, dropping less than 10%.\par \par \uc2 Solana\u8217\'20\'19s run puts the market on notice\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-traders-flock-to-solana-as-demand-for-eth-and-btc-flattens"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 institutional traders flocked to Solana}}}\uc2  as demand for Ether and Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) exposure seemed to plateau. In this regard, over the first week of September, SOL-centric investment products represented a whopping 86.6% of the total weekly inflows into the crypto investment market.\par \par \uc2 More specifically, per {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinshares.com/research/digital-asset-fund-flows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  made available by \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  management firm \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  recently, SOL\u8217\'20\'19s combined investment products {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/vol-46-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-bccdbbeaff99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 witnessed}}}\uc2  inflows in excess of $49.4 million between Sept. 6 and 10. Not only that, for the week, SOL saw a 275% week-over-week increase in its value, representing 86.6% of total capital inflow into the crypto investment sector.\par \par \uc2 Lastly, other \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  products have also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/institutional-exposure-to-altcoin-products-retests-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued to see major cash inflows}}}\uc2  for the fourth consecutive week, with demand for different altcoins quite easily exceeding that of BTC products, with the latter only witnessing minimal inflows of $200,000. For example, it is worth highlighting that during the first half of September, multi-asset products, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2 , Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s DOT and Bitcoin Cash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-cash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BCH}}}\uc2  ) were able to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/coinshares/vol-46-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-bccdbbeaff99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 register}}}\uc2  sizable financial inflows of fa$3.2 million, $3.1 million, $1.7 million and $600,000, respectively.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUndiscovered\u8221\'20\'1D projects pique institutional interest\par \par \uc2 Kadan Stadelmann, chief technical officer of end-to-end blockchain infrastructure solutions provider Komodo, told Cointelegraph that rising demand for undiscovered projects is nothing new for the crypto market. However, what separates this time from previous cycles is the sheer amount of capital flowing in from institutions. He said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe risk is that this will lead to faster market cycles for specific cryptocurrencies that are outliers from overall market movements. We see extreme FOMO and price increases, followed by a large sell-off and price declines. With SOL, in particular, prices are down 20% this week. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it won\u8217\'20\'19t quickly return back to its all-time high. It\u8217\'20\'19s just that people who are new to crypto should be aware that \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  is par for the course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lastly, echoing Trenchev\u8217\'20\'19s view, Stadelmann believes that as we move into an increasingly decentralized future, it will become more common to see a sharp increase in the price of different altcoins. \u8220\'20\'1CHundreds of DeFi projects are flying under the radar. Many of these projects have solid technology and can gain upward price momentum once institutions recognize their potential,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The rise of altcoins is justifiable\par \par \uc2 One of the core reasons underlying the rise of many of the above-stated altcoins has been the lack of scalability offered by the Ethereum network. In this regard, despite all of its recent highly touted functional updates, the platform is only able to process around 15\u8211\'20\'1325 transactions per second in its current state \u8212\'20\'14 all while offering an extremely low throughput capacity.\par \par \uc2 Not only that, even though the recently concluded London hard fork was designed to help regulate Ether\u8217\'20\'19s rising gas fees \u8212\'20\'14 after rates rose as high as $40 and $70 earlier this year during Q1 and Q2, respectively \u8212\'20\'14 the figure still seems to be hovering around the $15\u8211\'20\'13$20 range, which is quite high for the average Ethereum customer.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, during peak traffic hours, minting a nonfungible token (NFT) on the Ethereum network can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-killers-or-just-pretenders-ethereum-remains-king-for-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cost up to}}}\uc2  3 ETH, which, in many cases, may actually work out to a price point that is more than the actual NFT itself. On the other hand, Solana, as well as many other projects, not only offer faster transaction speeds but far lower gas prices, allowing for the more economical issuance of NFTs.\par \par \uc2 With Ethereum gearing up to make its transition to a proof-of-stake framework, it is expected that once the move is finally done, the platform will be able to process up to 100,000 transactions per second. However, until that day comes, it looks as though a growing list of smart contract-enabled platforms may continue to eat into Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s mammoth market share.\par \par \uc2 Is Ethereum on the verge of being overshadowed?\par \par \uc2 Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s most recent overhaul, the all-important London hard fork \u8212\'20\'14 which incidentally contained crucial updates such as the Ethereum Improvement Proposal 1559 \u8212\'20\'14 was supposed to deploy a new transaction pricing mechanism for the network, resulting in the ecosystem becoming deflationary in nature.\par \par \uc2 Available {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ultrasound.money/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  suggests that over 336,000 ETH tokens have already been burned, with the current burn rate currently sitting at 4.9 ETH per second or about 2.7 million ETH tokens per year, which would basically take the project\u8217\'20\'19s yearly supply growth rate to 2.3% while taking its issuance to around 5.3 million tokens per annum.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, Ethereum is not the only project to make use of such a deflationary setup, since Solana is also known to burn 50% of its transaction fees to regulate the supply of its native SOL token. Khalid Howladar, chairman of MRHB DeFi \u8212\'20\'14 a Shariah-compliant decentralized finance (DeFi) platform \u8212\'20\'14 told Cointelegraph:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that Ethereum is the current smart contract backbone of the DeFi ecosystem, Solana is emerging as a solid competitor with potentially more upside to come. Key factors such as cost and speed mean that Solana has become a solid challenger to Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s position both within the realm of programmable money (DeFi) and programmable media (NFTs).\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Howladar\u8217\'20\'19s view, institutions are only just getting their toes wet when it comes to DeFi, and therefore, the next few months could be extremely interesting in terms of how they become further involved. \u8220\'20\'1CIf DeFi platforms can somehow ensure basic things like consumer protection using decentralized KYC and AML, they will take vast chunks out of banks\u8217\'20\'19 market share, especially as peer-to-peer economic systems take hold,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Moving forward, it will be interesting to see whether Ethereum is able to maintain its current dominance levels, especially as a growing list of smart contract-enabled alternatives continues to garner mainstream market traction.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvNzk0Y2FmMmMtZGQ4Yy00NGJlLThmMzYtZTU0NGEzMzQzMmYxLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210921eh9l0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/20: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, UNI, AVAX\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,836 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and most major altcoins have dropped to their critical support levels, which is likely to attract strong buying from the bulls.\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets and the U.S. equity markets sold off on Sept. 20 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-loses-44k-support-as-stocks-evergrande-nerves-hit-btc-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on fears that the collapse}}}\uc2  of Chinese property giant Evergrande could not only hurt China but also have wider implications in other markets.\par \par \uc2 When the sentiment is \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders dump positions that they perceive as risky in favor of safe-haven trades. This could be one of the reasons for the sharp fall in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and most major altcoins on Sept. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/63eb36cc-197c-4343-8aaf-0d9cc7b835e3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Data from Bybt shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-drops-below-43k-as-binance-s-btc-stash-grows-to-may-crash-levels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin held in Binance wallets has surged}}}\uc2  by 29,717 Bitcoin in the past 30 days. History suggests that an increase in the Bitcoin balance on Binance has resulted in a drop in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price.\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin balance on Binance rose from 99,700 BTC on April 20 to 347,590 BTC on June 26. During this period, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price plunged from about $57,000 to roughly $30,000.\par \par \uc2 Now the question is, could the sell-off deepen or will lower levels attract aggressive buying from traders? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s selling exacerbated after bears pulled the price below the moving averages. The price action of the past few days has formed a head and shoulders pattern that will complete on a breakdown and close below the neckline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/906bdde5-a34b-4088-9cec-8d59ec395f64.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages are on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the relative strength index (RSI) has dropped below 41, indicating that bears are in control. If the price sustains below the neckline, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to $37,332.70 and then to the pattern target of $32,423.05.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the neckline, the bulls will again try to push the price toward $50,000. However, the bears are likely to defend the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($47,014) aggressively.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this resistance, it will indicate that sentiment has turned negative and traders are selling on rallies. The first sign of strength will be a break and close above $48,843.20.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) bounced off the support at $3,377.89 on Sept. 18, but the bulls could not sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($3,402). This indicates that traders closed positions at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/02cbdca0-671d-46e6-a3ab-e4b59904ec7d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price breaks and closes below $3,000, the ETH/USDT pair will complete a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head and shoulders pattern. The target objective of this setup is $1,972.12.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI is below 42, indicating that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if bulls defend the $3,000 level aggressively, the pair could again rise toward the overhead resistance at $3,377.89. The bears are likely to defend this level but if bulls overcome this resistance, it will signal that the correction may be over.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls defended the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($2.31) on Sept. 18 but could not build on the rebound. Sustained selling pulled Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) below the 50-day SMA on Sept. 19.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/5973ae1a-09ba-4c33-8618-88ea9f920bac.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling escalated on Sept. 20 and the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair plunged to critical support at $1.94. The strong rebound off this level suggests that bulls are accumulating on dips.\par \par \uc2 If buyers sustain the bounce, the pair could gradually move up toward the overhead resistance at $2.47. The bears are likely to sell on relief rallies to the 20-day EMA ($2.45). If the price turns down from this resistance, the pair could again drop to $1.94.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above the 20-day EMA will be the first sign that the sellers may be losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) broke below the 50-day SMA ($422) on Sept. 17 and subsequent attempts by the bulls to reclaim the level failed. This suggests that bears are selling on every minor rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/6fd4638e-eb47-4621-a228-613b0b724ab0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling picked up momentum on Sept. 20 and the BNB/USDT pair dropped close to the critical support at $340. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break below it could open the doors for a decline to $300 and then $250.\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the negative zone, indicating that bears have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off $340, the pair could rise to the 20-day EMA. This level is likely to act as a stiff resistance. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above $422.80 to indicate that the correction may be over.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) had been trading near the breakout level at $1.07 for the past few days, but the failure of the bulls to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($1.09) showed that bears were selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/285c18f9-7847-4d08-a5e0-96a667d726f3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling intensified after the bears pulled and closed the price below the 50-day SMA ($1.08) on Sept. 19. The moving averages are on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI has dropped into the negative zone, indicating that bears are in command.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below $0.95, the XRP/USDT pair could drop to $0.75. Any relief rally from the current level is likely to face stiff resistance at the 20-day EMA. A breakout and close above $1.13 will signal that bulls are attempting a comeback.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long tail on the Sept. 17 candlestick shows that bulls aggressively bought the dip below the 20-day EMA ($148). That was followed by a strong bounce of Sept. 18 but the bulls could not sustain Solana (SOL) above the first resistance at $170.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/b435c9f9-0651-4092-b3dc-37de227d2387.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This may have attracted profit-booking from bulls and shorting from aggressive bears. The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the RSI is close to the midpoint, indicating that bulls are losing their grip.\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the SOL/USDT pair could drop to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $123.42. A break and close below this support will suggest that the uptrend could be over.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above $171.47 to signal the end of the corrective phase.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot\u8217\'20\'19s (DOT) rebound off the 20-day EMA ($32.12) on Sept. 18 was followed by an inside-day candlestick pattern on Sept. 19. This showed indecision among the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/4aa2a948-079f-47ef-a886-8afa24039e64.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This uncertainty resolved to the downside on Sept. 20 with a break below the 20-day EMA. The selling picked up momentum and dropped to critical support at the 50-day SMA ($27.29). This is an important support for the bulls because they had successfully defended it on Sept. 7.\par \par \uc2 If the DOT/USDT pair rebounds off the current level, the bears are likely to sell on rallies to the 20-day EMA. If the price turns down from this level, it will suggest that the sentiment has turned negative and that will increase the prospects of a break below the 50-day SMA. This negative view will invalidate if the price turns up and rises above $34.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-forming-a-double-top-eth-price-loses-12-5-amid-evergrande-contagion-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum forming a double top? ETH price loses 12.5% amid Evergrande contagion fears}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) tight range trading of the past few days resolved to the downside on Sept. 20 as bears pulled the price to the strong support at $0.21.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/386d6d4d-7ef4-4338-99c1-27f20ef452fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The falling 20-day EMA ($0.25) and the RSI near the oversold territory indicate that bears are in control. If they can sink and sustain the price below the $0.21 support, the DOGE/USDT pair could slide to $0.15.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level, the bulls will again try to push the pair above the 20-day EMA. If they manage to do that, the pair could rise to the downtrend line. Alternatively, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will increase the prospects of a break below $0.21.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls attempted a recovery on Sept. 18 but could not push Uniswap (UNI) above the 20-day EMA ($25.09). This showed that bears are aggressively defending the 20-day EMA.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/6e09fc7b-4c9d-4c5c-af9c-dde2df39d434.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The UNI/USDT pair continued lower and the bears pulled the price below the critical support at $21 today. If the price sustains below this support, the pair could witness panic selling and decline to the next support at $18.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone indicate an advantage to bears. This negative view will invalidate if the price turns up from the current level and rises above the downtrend line. Such a move will indicate strong accumulation at lower levels.\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT\par \par \uc2 The long wick on the Sept. 18 and 19 candlestick showed that traders were booking profits at higher levels. The selling intensified today and Avalanche (AVAX) dropped to the 20-day EMA ($55.16).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e63f0ca6-988b-41fa-bf44-901f9ad8e02d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The strong rebound off the 20-day EMA suggests that sentiment remains positive and traders are accumulating on dips. If the price sustains above $60.04, the bulls will again attempt to push the AVAX/USDT pair toward the all-time high at $76.27.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the 20-day EMA, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could pick up as traders may rush to the exit. That could pull the price down to $48 and then to the 50-day SMA ($38.56) where buyers may step in to arrest the decline.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvY2M1MzFhYzctMTdjMi00YzUyLWI5YzItN2VhMzNmMTU5MzI3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210921eh9k00039\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ethereum\par \b \uc2 Ethereum forming a double top? ETH price loses 12.5% amid Evergrande contagion fears\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 807 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The latest bout of selling in the Ethereum market also triggered a classic \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern, which has a 75% accuracy in hitting its downside targets.\par \par \uc2 Prices of Ethereum's native asset, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), slumped on Sept. 20 amid a broad sell-off in the cryptocurrency market, led by worries about a potential housing bubble crisis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/best-bear-market-ever-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brewing in China}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USD exchange rate dropped as much as 12.52% to $2,911 on the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  exchange, hitting its lowest levels since the beginning of August. Elsewhere in the crypto market, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana (SOL) and other top tokens plunged in tandem.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e4af08f2-d1e6-4f5b-b206-f6119249dcbf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The performance of top 10 crypto assets in the past 24 hours. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 The drop imitated the mood in the broader market as United States equities plunged following a day of red in both the Asia-Pacific and European indexes. On the other hand, the U.S. dollar and government bonds surged on haven-buying.\par \par \uc2 At the core of Monday's sell-off was a liquidity crisis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-loses-44k-support-as-stocks-evergrande-nerves-hit-btc-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese property developer Evergrande}}}\uc2 . The world\u8217\'20\'19s most indebted property developer faces obligations of more than $300 billion to creditors. That also includes a critical interest payment deadline on its offshore bonds, arriving on Sept. 23.\par \par \uc2 DW noted that if Evergrande topples, it could bring many banks down with it, same as \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  did during 2008's housing bubble crisis in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Although Ether does not trade in sync with global markets, its 30-day correlation with Bitcoin \u8212\'20\'14 the leading \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposed to macroeconomic fundamentals \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptowat.ch/correlations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sits near 0.85}}}\uc2 . As a result, the altcoin appeared to have faced an indirect consequence of China's looming housing crisis.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern triggered\par \par \uc2 The latest bout of selling in the Ether market also triggered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://samuraitradingacademy.com/7-best-price-action-patterns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classic \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22  pattern, which has a 75% accuracy}}}\uc2  when it comes to hitting its downside targets.\par \par \uc2 Dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1Cdouble top,\u8221\'20\'1D the pattern develops after the price rallies strongly, pulls back, rises again toward the previous peak and corrects all over again \u8212\'20\'14 all while standing atop the so-called neckline support. Ultimately, the price falls below the neckline and targets levels located as deep as the distance between the double top's peak and the neckline.\par \par \uc2 Ether appears to be halfway through while painting a double top pattern. The cryptocurrency's chart below shows that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-liquidity-crisis-could-see-new-eth-all-time-high-before-bitcoin-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 topped near $4,385}}}\uc2  on May 12, fell toward the neckline support of $1,984 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/2-key-ethereum-price-metrics-back-traders-confidence-in-3-800-eth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rose back to another sessional peak of $4,030}}}\uc2  on Sept. 3.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ebed696a-f28a-45c9-9e21-796d0d5076dc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD weekly price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the double top pattern flourishes, ETH/USD rates could extend their ongoing sell-off toward $1,984 for a potential breakdown move afterward. Nonetheless, it does not look feasible for ETH/USD to drop aggressively below the $1,984-neckline.\par \par \uc2 The level is also near Ether's 50-week exponential moving average (EMA) (the velvet wave) currently at $2,118, offering another support layer to safeguard Ether's \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  bias. Earlier, the wave acted as an entrylevel for bulls following sharper ETH/USD pullbacks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-killers-or-just-pretenders-ethereum-remains-king-for-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum killers or just pretenders? But Ether remains king for now}}}\par \par \uc2 At the same time, on a daily timeframe, the next support line for Ether appears near its 200-day EMA (the orange wave) at $2,536. Thus, a sharp pullback from the said level could negate the double top setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/d7f77255-ee3c-4543-b4a6-0d85b2db3acf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily price chart featuring 200-day EMA support. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Fundamentals\par \par \uc2 Ether continues to eye adoption against Ethereum's role in backing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-is-great-but-real-crypto-innovation-has-moved-elsewhere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 booming decentralized finance}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-is-great-but-real-crypto-innovation-has-moved-elsewhere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-is-great-but-real-crypto-innovation-has-moved-elsewhere}}}\uc2  (DeFi) and nonfungible token (NFT) industry. In the recent SALT conference, Cathie Wood, CEO of Ark Invest, also said that investors should allocate at least 40% of their crypto portfolios to Ether.\par \par \uc2 Ark Investment CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CathieDWood?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CathieDWood}}}\uc2  's confidence in Ethereum and Bitcoin is growing.\par \par \uc2 Projecting a 10x growth rate over the next five years, the firm\u8217\'20\'19s crypto exposure is likely to be split: 60% BTC and 40% ETH. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VQCZhVCD3m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VQCZhVCD3m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cointelegraph (@Cointelegraph) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Cointelegraph/status/1438268943169474563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Excerpts from Wood's statement include:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m fascinated with what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in DeFi, which is collapsing the cost of the infrastructure for financial services in a way that I know that the traditional financial industry does not appreciate right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvMjA2ZGQxYWUtYjZmYi00YjQ0LWJmNDMtMDA2Y2JiYjFlMjA3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210921eh9k0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ethereum\par \b \uc2 Ethereum forming a double top? ETH price loses 12.5% amid Evergrande contagion fears\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Yashu Gola \par \uc2 798 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The latest bout of selling in the Ethereum market also triggered a classic \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern, which has a 75% accuracy in hitting its downside targets.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum's native asset Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) prices slumped on Sept. 20 amid a broad selloff in the cryptocurrency market, led by worries about a potential housing bubble crisis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/best-bear-market-ever-5-things-to-watch-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brewing in China}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USD exchange rate dropped as much as 12.52% to $2,911 on the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  exchange, hitting its lowest levels since the beginning of August 2021. Elsewhere in the crypto market, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana (SOL), and other top tokens plunged in tandem.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e4af08f2-d1e6-4f5b-b206-f6119249dcbf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The performance of top ten crypto assets in the past 24 hours. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 The drop imitated the mood in the broader market as United States equities plunged following a day of red in both the Asia-Pacific and European indexes. On the other hand, the U.S. dollar and government bonds surged on haven-buying.\par \par \uc2 At the core of Monday's sell-off was a liquidity crisis at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-loses-44k-support-as-stocks-evergrande-nerves-hit-btc-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese property developer Evergrande}}}\uc2 . The world\u8217\'20\'19s most indebted property developer faces obligations of more than $300 billion to creditors. That also includes a critical interest payment deadline on its offshore bonds, arriving on Sept. 23.\par \par \uc2 DW noted that if the Evergrande topples, it could bring many banks down with it, same as the Lehman brothers did during the 2008's housing bubble crisis in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Although Ether does not trade in sync with global markets, its 30-day correlation with Bitcoin, the leading \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposed to macroeconomic fundamentals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptowat.ch/correlations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sits near 0.85}}}\uc2 . As a result, the altcoin appeared to have faced an indirect consequence to China's looming housing crisis.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern triggered\par \par \uc2 The latest bout of selling in the Ethereum market also triggered a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://samuraitradingacademy.com/7-best-price-action-patterns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 classic \b  \highlight22bearish\b0 \highlight22  pattern, which has a 75% accuracy}}}\uc2  when it comes to hitting its downside targets.\par \par \uc2 Dubbed the "Double Top,' the pattern develops after the price rallies strongly, pulls back, rises again towards the previous peak, and corrects all over again \u8212\'20\'14 all while standing atop the so-called neckline support. Ultimately, the price falls below the neckline and targets levels located as deep as the distance between Double Top's peak and the neckline.\par \par \uc2 Ether appears to be halfway through while painting a Double Top pattern. The cryptocurrency's chart below shows that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-liquidity-crisis-could-see-new-eth-all-time-high-before-bitcoin-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 topped near $4,385}}}\uc2  on May 12, fell towards the neckline support of $1,984 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/2-key-ethereum-price-metrics-back-traders-confidence-in-3-800-eth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rose back to another sessional peak of $4,030}}}\uc2  on Sept. 3.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ebed696a-f28a-45c9-9e21-796d0d5076dc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD weekly price chart. Source: TradingView.com\par \par \uc2 If the Double Top pattern flourishes, the ETH/USD rates could extend their ongoing selloff toward $1,984 for a potential breakdown move afterward. Nonetheless, it does not look feasible for ETH/USD to drop aggressively below the $1,984-neckline.\par \par \uc2 The level is also near the Ether's 50-week exponential moving average (EMA) (the velvet wave) currently at $2,118, offering another support layer to safeguard Ether's \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  bias. Earlier, the wave acted as an entry-level for bulls following sharper ETH/USD pullbacks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-killers-or-just-pretenders-ethereum-remains-king-for-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum killers or just pretenders? But Ether remains king for now}}}\par \par \uc2 At the same time, on a daily timeframe, the next support line for Ether appears near its 200-day EMA (the orange wave) at $2,536. Thus, a sharp pullback from the said level could negate the Double Top setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/d7f77255-ee3c-4543-b4a6-0d85b2db3acf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily price chart featuring 200-day EMA support. Source: TradingView.com\par \par \uc2 Fundamentals\par \par \uc2 Ether continues to eye adoption against Ethereum's role in backing the booming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-is-great-but-real-crypto-innovation-has-moved-elsewhere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized finance}}}\uc2  (DeFi) and nonfungible token (NFT) industry. In the recent SALT conference, Cathie Wood, the CEO of Ark Invest, also said that investors should allocate at least 40% of their crypto portfolios to Ether.\par \par \uc2 Ark Investment CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CathieDWood?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CathieDWood}}}\uc2  's confidence in Ethereum and Bitcoin is growing.\par \par \uc2 Projecting a 10x growth rate over the next five years, the firm\u8217\'20\'19s crypto exposure is likely to be split: 60% BTC and 40% ETH. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VQCZhVCD3m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VQCZhVCD3m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cointelegraph (@Cointelegraph) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Cointelegraph/status/1438268943169474563?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Excerpts from Wood's statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m fascinated with what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in DeFi, which is collapsing the cost of the infrastructure for financial services in a way that I know that the traditional financial industry does not appreciate right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph.com. Every investment and trading move involves risk, you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvMjA2ZGQxYWUtYjZmYi00YjQ0LWJmNDMtMDA2Y2JiYjFlMjA3LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210920eh9k0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ethereum\par \b \uc2 Ethereum killers or just pretenders? But Ether remains king for now\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Anirudh Tiwari \par \uc2 1,384 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The issue of high gas fees rears its head up for the Ethereum community yet again as \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum killer\u8221\'20\'1D networks continue to gain more attention.\par \par \uc2 The term \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum killer\u8221\'20\'1D is beginning to pick up the pace once again in the cryptocurrency markets as the native tokens of several competing blockchain networks are posting significant gains during September. For any alternative network to be considered as a part of this category, it needs to have one essential feature that serves as the backbone of the Ethereum network: smart contracts.\par \par \uc2 Keeping this in mind, the most prominent blockchain networks by market capitalization that usually come under this purview are Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana (SOL), Binance Smart Chain (BSC), Polkadot (DOT), and Terra(LUNA). The native tokens of these networks have been on an absolute tear this year. Most recently, Solana (SOL) has been in the spotlight after the bulls carrying its rally continued even in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-sharp-fall-from-50k-linked-to-stronger-us-dollar-gold-correlation-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 face of a marketwide selloff}}}\uc2  on Sept. 8 that brought Bitcoin back below the $50,000 mark.\par \par \uc2 SOL has more than doubled in price over the last 30 days but has since declined to trade around the $155 mark. The token has posted over 300% gains over the last 90 days with an extraordinary 7,871.16% gains year-to-date (YTD). In comparison, these gains dwarf ETH\u8217\'20\'19s 63.77% 90-day gains and 385.36% YTD gains. Ethereum's market capitalization is currently at around $400 billion which is nearly 9 times SOL\u8217\'20\'19s $47 billion market cap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/869ab827-53ce-47d0-99c3-b3274effcf3e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum killer tokens post gains\par \par \uc2 Several networks have shown promising prospects and gains. Cardano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-launches-smart-contracts-after-successful-hard-fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently completed its Alonzo hard fork}}}\uc2  that launched Plutus-powered smart contracts on the network that would allow it to host decentralized finance (DeFi) and Web 3.0 applications. Even though its native token, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , showed a lackluster response to this milestone in the project\u8217\'20\'19s roadmap, it has still experienced a substantial rise this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades at around $2.40, posting 74.16% gains in the last 90 days and 1,273.86% gains YTD.\par \par \uc2 Marie Tatibouet, chief marketing officer at Gate.io \u8212\'20\'14 a cryptocurrency exchange \u8212\'20\'14 outlined to Cointelegraph the twofold reasons that started the Ethereum killer movement. Speaking about the network\u8217\'20\'19s lack of scalability, she said, \u8220\'20\'1CAs things stand, Ethereum is particularly slow and can only do 15-25 transactions per second with very low throughput.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She further mentioned how high demand and low throughput lead to the next reason, bloated transaction fees that \u8220\'20\'1Care a bit of control.\u8221\'20\'1D This could go on to have an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/the-ongoing-nft-boom-can-supply-of-nonfungibles-outweigh-demand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impact on the ongoing boom}}}\uc2  seen in the nonfungible token (NFT) market. She said, \u8220\'20\'1CDo you really want to pay half an ETH in gas fees just to mint a JPEG?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On this, Solana Labs spokesperson told Cointelegraph, \u8220\'20\'1CMinting an NFT at peak levels can be very costly. Recently, a minting fee hit 3 ETH, which is more expensive than many actual NFTs. Solana offers faster speeds and lower prices than Ethereum, which is really what it comes down to with market shares.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another Ethereum killer prospect whose token has witnessed an outstanding performance this year is Terra. Its native token LUNA posted over 500% gains in the last 90 days and 5,477% gains YTD, and is currently trading at around $36.\par \par \uc2 Such significant gains often put a token into the spotlight due to its underlying platform and technology getting more users and increasing adoption rates. Cointelegraph spoke with Lex Sokolin, global fintech co-head and head economist at ConSensys \u8212\'20\'14 a blockchain technology company backing Ethereum's infrastructure \u8212\'20\'14 who stated:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDeFi protocols are applications that grow with the number of users and capital. It is likely that DeFi will be multichain and multipurpose, though the largest amount of liquidity will remain secured by Ethereum. However, expanding and incorporating other capital sources through bridges and exchanges is a net good for the ecosystem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ethereum is currently in an important stage of its transformation to Ethereum 2.0 (Eth2) \u8212\'20\'14 an entirely proof-of-stake (PoS) blockchain after undergoing the London hard fork that brought in crucial updates like the EIP-1559 \u8212\'20\'14 the aftermath of which is still highly discussed in the cryptocurrency community. This Ethereum Improvement Proposal (EIP) that was agreed upon by the developers, and miners entailed a change in the transaction pricing mechanism for the network.\par \par \uc2 The change mainly impacted the inflation rate of the tokens and the miner\u8217\'20\'19s revenues since a portion of gas fees are now being burned following the upgrade. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ultrasound.money"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2 , over 311,300 ETH tokens have been burned, with a notional value of nearly $1.1 billion. The current burn rate is 2.7 million ETH tokens per year, which would put the inflation rate at 2.3% with the issuance of 5.3 million tokens per year.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum is not the only blockchain network to implement this kind of pricing mechanism, as Solana burns 50% of its transaction fees to regulate the supply of the SOL token. The Solana Labs spokesperson further said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Ethereum London upgrade changed miner incentives. Some believed that this would increase the MEV and there have been solutions launched to address this, but the cost of transactions on Ethereum continues to provide a barrier to entry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On-chain data says Ethereum is still king\par \par \uc2 Even though the native tokens of these \u8220\'20\'1CEthereum killer\u8221\'20\'1D networks have posted impressive gains, a closer look at the on-chain data reveals that Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s utilization and volumes still dwarf the entirety of the remaining smart contract platform market.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum currently has a market capitalization of over $400 billion, which is significantly higher than the rest of the market. The closest network in terms of market cap is Cardano, with a $76 billion market capitalization, not even 20% as that of Ethereum.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dappradar.com/defi/protocol/ethereum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According}}}\uc2  to data by DappRadar, the total volume locked (TVL) in DeFi protocols built on the Ethereum blockchain is just over $100 billion. In terms of utilization, the blockchain network that ranks second is the Binance Smart Chain (BSC) with a TVL of $18 billion, less than 20% of Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s TVL in DeFi.\par \par \uc2 BSC ecosystem coordinator at Binance cryptocurrency exchange Samy Karim spoke to Cointelegraph about the possibilities of Ethereum retaining its market share once the transition to Eth2 is complete:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt has to be quick, efficient and decentralized at the same time for DeFi to attain mass adoption. Ethereum is one of the first smart contract compatible chains that can leverage its pre-existing communities to grow once Eth2 is out, but it\u8217\'20\'19s next to impossible to forecast its potential market share on the basis of its probable upgrade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Currently, Ethereum leads the market in the NFT space as well with all the biggest NFT platforms, OpenSea, CryptoPunks, Axie Infinity, Rarible and Decentraland all being built on Ethereum. However, the whole NFT market has often been classified as a bubble by naysayers with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/chinese-communist-party-warn-of-nft-hype-bubble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese Communist Party becoming the latest addition}}}\uc2  when it warned the Chinese citizens about digital collectibles, and, yet, the market continues to expand.\par \par \uc2 Sokolin has voiced his disagreement on this perspective, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe disagree with the categorization of the NFT ecosystem as a bubble \u8212\'20\'14 it is a reconfiguration of digital media structure. [...] NFTs offer a different path and having a meaningful economic system is unlocking a new business model.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, the impact of this \u8220\'20\'1Cbubble\u8221\'20\'1D even going \u8220\'20\'1Cbust\u8221\'20\'1D is limited for Ethereum. In Tatibouet\u8217\'20\'19s opinion, \u8220\'20\'1CNFTs or not, Ethereum is still the market leader when it comes to smart contract platforms. The NFT market, however, has helped the competitors in gaining an advantage over their peers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Ethereum continues to build momentum toward its final transition to a PoS blockchain, the confidence that the financial markets are showing in its potential is slowly rising. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tbstat.com/wp/uploads/2021/09/Ethereum-investor-guide.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by the British multinational bank, Standard Chartered Bank, discussed the real-world use cases of the blockchain network and accordingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tbstat.com/wp/uploads/2021/09/Ethereum-investor-guide.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 valued}}}\uc2  ETH \u8220\'20\'1Cstructurally\u8221\'20\'1D between $26,000 and $35,000. As of now, ETH continues to show \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading patterns such as cup and handle and even has the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-eyes-6-5k-bullish-target-as-eth-price-chart-paints-cup-and-handle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prospect of hitting $6,500}}}\uc2  in the coming few months.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvZDhkNzdkN2YtNTdmYi00Mzk0LTllZGYtYjVhNGE4MWJiODEwLmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210920eh9j0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Hodler's\par \b \uc2 Cardano price dips after smart contract launch, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  working with \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  is fake news, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  raises $2B from junk-bond sale: Hodler\u8217\'20\'19s Digest, Sept. 12-18\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Editorial Staff \par \uc2 1,883 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coming every Saturday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/hodlers-digest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hodlers Digest}}}\uc2  will help you track every single important news story that happened this week. The best (and worst) quotes, adoption and \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlights, leading coins, predictions and much more a week on Cointelegraph in one link.\par \par \uc2 Top Stories This Week\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-launches-smart-contracts-after-successful-hard-fork"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano launches smart contracts after successful hard fork}}}\par \par \uc2 After years of anticipation, Charles Hoskinsons brainchild, Cardano, finally launched its smart contract functionality via the Alonzo hard fork on Monday. Youd think the result of this would be some \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price action for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  but, alas, its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sell-the-news-ada-price-drops-10-following-cardano-s-long-awaited-smart-contracts-rollout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 price dropped 10%}}}\uc2  following the rollout.\par \par \uc2 While Cardano was keen to celebrate the milestone, it also emphasized in a blog post that its still in the early days of the project, adding that now is when the mission truly begins.\par \par \uc2 The team also urged its community to not be overzealous in boarding the hype train just yet, and to be patient with the smart contract functionality in its formative stages:\par \par \uc2 There are high expectations resting on this upgrade. Some unreasonably so. Cardano watchers may be expecting a sophisticated ecosystem of consumer-ready DApps available immediately after the upgrade. Expectations need to be managed here.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fake-news-litecoin-price-surges-35-following-walmart-adoption-hoax"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fake news: Litecoin price surges 35% following Walmart adoption hoax}}}\par \par \uc2 While real news made the price of \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop, fake news made the price of \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) pump this week.\par \par \uc2 Numerous publications reported Monday that \uc2 Walmart\uc2  planned to have a pay with \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  option for its e-commerce websites starting on Oct. 1 as part of a partnership with the Litecoin Foundation. Following the spread of the fake report, the price of LTC surged 35% before sharply falling within hours.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson from \uc2 Walmart\uc2  confirmed that the news was fake within an hour, while the Litecoin Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s director of marketing, Jay Milla, also told Cointelegraph that the announcement did not come from Litcecoin\u8217\'20\'19s side of things.\par \par \uc2 The Litecoin Foundation has yet to enter into a partnership with \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , said Milla.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/vitalik-buterin-makes-list-of-time-magazine-s-100-most-influential-people-in-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vitalik Buterin makes list of Time magazines 100 most influential people in 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin was named by Time Magazine as one of the 100 most influential people of this year, joining the likes of Naomi Osaka, Britney Spears, Xi Jinping and Elon Musk.\par \par \uc2 Buterin was featured in the Innovators section of the Time 100 list, with Reddit co-founder Alexis Ohanian authoring his profile. Ohanian highlighted Buterins work in building the Ethereum network and encouraging the development of decentralized apps and NFTs.\par \par \uc2 No one person couldve possibly come up with all of the uses for Ethereum, but it did take one persons idea to get it started, Ohanian said. From there, a new world has opened up, and given rise to new ways of leveraging blockchain technology.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-increases-junk-bond-offering-to-2b-after-investors-swarm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase increases junk-bond offering to $2B after investors swarm}}}\par \par \uc2 After seeing enormous demand for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-coinbase-plans-to-raise-1-5b-via-debt-offering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.5 billion junk-bond}}}\uc2  offering that was announced on Monday, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  reportedly increased the size of the sale to $2 billion.\par \par \uc2 According to a report from The Economic Times, there was at least $7 billion worth of orders that were placed in competition for seven- and 10-year bonds offering interest rates of 3.375% and 3.625%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  stated on Monday that the raised funds will be put towards continued investments in product developments and potential investments in or acquisitions of other companies, products, or technologies in the future.\par \par \uc2 The funds might also come in handy when the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, or SEC, comes knocking on the door with a lawsuit if the USD coin lending program is actually launched.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-lawmakers-propose-adding-digital-assets-to-wash-sale-rule-and-raising-capital-gains-tax"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US lawmakers propose adding digital assets to wash sale rule and raising capital gains tax}}}\par \par \uc2 Reports surfaced this week that Democrats in the \uc2 U.S. House of Representatives\uc2  proposed tax initiatives that could swipe some extra profits from the gains of certain high-income crypto users.\par \par \uc2 According to a document released by the House Committee on Ways and Means on Monday, the proposal would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://waysandmeans.house.gov/sites/democrats.waysandmeans.house.gov/files/documents/SubtitleISxS.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase}}}\uc2  the tax rate on long-term capital gains from the existing 20% to 25%.\par \par \uc2 On the same day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/president-biden-announces-picks-to-fill-cftc-vacancies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Joe Biden}}}\uc2  said he planned to nominate acting chairman of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, Rostin Behnam, to assume the role permanently, while also naming Kristin Johnson and Christy Goldsmith Romero to fill two other vacant commissioner seats.\par \par \uc2 In a private meeting held on Sept. 8 between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fidelity-lobbies-sec-to-approve-bitcoin-etf-in-private-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fidelity Digital Assets}}}\uc2  President Tom Jessop, six of the firms executives and several SEC officials, the executives outlined a number of reasons why the enforcer should finally approve the Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) exchange-traded fund.\par \par \uc2 These examples included increased demand for digital assets, the prevalence of similar funds in other countries, and the rise of Bitcoin adoption all of which sound like reasons that would fall on deaf ears for the SEC.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Digest_17-09_1-1024x682.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Winners and Losers\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Winners-and-Losers_sept_12-18-1024x826.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 At the end of the week, Bitcoin is at $46,951, Ether at $3,376 and XRP at $1.07. The total market cap is at $2.11 trillion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to CoinMarketCap.\par \par \uc2 Among the biggest 100 cryptocurrencies, the top three altcoin gainers of the week are Curve DAO Token (CRV) at 41.73%, Hedera Hashgraph (HBAR) at 41.16% and Avalanche (AVAX) at 33.23%.\par \par \uc2 The top three altcoin losers of the week are Arweave (AR) at -19.24%, Solana (SOL) at -21.27% and Revain (REV) at -17.11%.\par \par \uc2 For more info on crypto prices, make sure to read {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/markets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cointelegraphs market analysis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most Memorable Quotations\par \par \uc2 Many platforms have dozens or hundreds of tokens on them. While each tokens legal status depends on its own facts and circumstances, the probability is quite remote that, with 50, 100, or 1,000 tokens, any given platform has zero securities.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-chair-doubles-down-tells-crypto-firms-come-in-and-talk-to-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gary Gensler}}}\uc2 , U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission chairman\par \par \uc2 One can even see an inscription about the regulators obligations on the banknotes, while cryptocurrency is not backed by anything.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uzbekistan-has-no-plans-to-ease-crypto-payments-ban-says-official"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Behzod Khamraev}}}\uc2 , Central Bank of Uzbekistan deputy chairman\par \par \uc2 Advocates say crypto markets are all about financial inclusion, but the people who are most economically vulnerable are the ones who are most likely to have to withdraw their money the fastest when the market drops. [\u8230\'20\'26] High, unpredictable fees can make crypto trading really dangerous for people who arent rich.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sen-warren-goes-after-ethereum-network-fees-in-committee-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren}}}\uc2 , U.S. senator\par \par \uc2 Rising valuations across asset classes, massive price swings in cryptoassets and event-driven risks observed in 1H21 amid elevated trading volumes raise questions about increased risk-taking behaviour and possible market exuberance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/eu-regulator-sees-crypto-as-sign-of-increased-risk-taking-in-current-climate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The European Securities and Markets Authority}}}\par \par \uc2 Its a no-brainer that your crypto earnings are taxable like other income and should be declared in the Income Tax Returns. As of now, it is not clear whether the GST would be applied on the amount of cryptocurrency bought or on the transaction fees paid by the user.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/india-s-income-tax-department-may-soon-target-crypto-trades-and-ecosystem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nischal Shetty}}}\uc2 , WazirX CEO\par \par \uc2 If a person has assets in Bitcoin and makes high profits, there will be no tax. This is done obviously to encourage foreign investment.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-investors-are-reportedly-exempt-from-taxes-in-el-salvador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Javier Argueta}}}\uc2 , legal adviser to El Salvadors president, Nayib Bukele\par \par \uc2 While it might be helpful for the SEC to provide advisory guidance to companies, it has no obligation to do so.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/regulatory-and-privacy-concerns-trail-sec-s-threat-to-coinbase"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marc Powers}}}\uc2 , former SEC Division of Enforcement officer\par \par \uc2 In a situation where the relevant taxation infrastructure is not sufficiently established, the deferral of taxation on virtual assets is not an option, but an inevitable situation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korean-lawmaker-delaying-tax-laws-on-crypto-is-inevitable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Noh Woong-rae}}}\uc2 , South Korea National Assembly member\par \par \uc2 Prediction of the Week\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-bitcoin-price-model-suggests-btc-won-t-go-below-39k-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Bitcoin price model suggests BTC won\u8217\'20\'19t go below $39K again}}}\par \par \uc2 Analyst William Clemente came up with a new metric for Bitcoin price boundary forecasts, posting the tool on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this week. Called the Illiquid Supply Floor, the chart merges PlanBs stock-to-flow metric and on-chain Bitcoin supply data from Glassnode. The result? A chart showing Bitcoins current price against the backdrop of possible upper and lower price range boundaries.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoins price rallied this week, showing recovery after the asset took a sizable dive down to the $43,000 range during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/2021/09/11/el-salvador-bitcoin-law-101-bored-ape-nfts-ukraine-passes-crypto-legislation-hodlers-digest-sept-5-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the week of Sept. 7}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to Clementes chart, the $39,000 price range could be the current bottom limit for Bitcoins price should it drop once again, given a price floor based on Bitcoins real-time scarcity Clementes description of the lower limit on the chart.\par \par \uc2 FUD of the Week\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Digest_17-09_2-1024x682.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/solana-and-arbitrum-knocked-offline-while-ethereum-evades-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana and Arbitrum knocked offline, while Ethereum evades attack}}}\par \par \uc2 The recent Solana-rama was temporarily brought to a halt this week after the supposed ETH killer suffered a denial-of-service disruption for around 45 minutes.\par \par \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account Solana Status explained that a large increase in transaction load to 400,000 per second overwhelmed the network, creating the denial-of-service and causing the network to start forking. The incident appears to have slightly damped enthusiasm in SOL, as the price is down 26% over the past seven days.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum layer-two rollup network Arbitrum One also reported its sequencer had gone offline for roughly 45 minutes this week, while Ethereum was also the subject of an unsuccessful node attack from an unknown identity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/opensea-exec-used-the-platform-s-influence-to-pump-his-own-nfts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OpenSea exec used the platforms influence to pump his own NFTs}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, OpenSea head of product Nathan Chastain was named and shamed after he was outed for hyping NFTs he purchased and then featuring them on the homepage of the popular marketplace.\par \par \uc2 While being \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on NFTs is nothing new, getting caught for tokenized insider trading is and Nathan Chastain is estimated to have earned at least 18.875 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), $65,700 at time of writing, from his antics.\par \par \uc2 OpenSea officially confirmed the accusations on Wednesday, noting that it was incredibly disappointing, and emphasized that the behavior did not represent the firms values. Chastain then proceeded to hand in his resignation the following day with his tail between his legs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/protesters-burn-bitcoin-atm-as-part-of-demonstration-against-el-salvador-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protesters burn Bitcoin ATM as part of demonstration against El Salvador president}}}\par \par \uc2 Anti-Bitcoiners and protesters of El Savador President Nayib Bukeles policies destroyed a BTC ATM in the nations capital city on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Local news outlets shared images of the ATM burning in San Salvador within a crowd of journalists and protesters. The booth hosting the BTC ATM was defaced with anti-BTC graffiti and a sign saying democracy is not for sale.\par \par \uc2 Despite maintaining a strong approval rating, Bukele appears to have caused a stir with his forceful approach to politics. There have now been multiple protests in El Salvador regarding adoption of BTC, with activists taking the streets as early as July to voice their concerns.\par \par \uc2 Best Cointelegraph Features\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Digest_17-09_3-1024x682.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/finding-a-new-home-bitcoin-miners-settling-down-after-china-exodus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Finding a new home: Bitcoin miners settling down after China exodus}}}\par \par \uc2 Countries vie for cryptocurrency miner business as Chinese miners move to greener pastures. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where they are ending up.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/el-salvador-s-bitcoin-day-the-first-of-many-or-a-one-off"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin day: The first of many or a one-off?}}}\par \par \uc2 Thanks to El Salvadors daring move, digital money looms large on global policymakers radars.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/2021/09/13/fidenza-tyler-hobbs-wrote-a-program-to-make-art-that-is-now-worth-millions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fidenza: Tyler Hobbs wrote software that generates art worth millions}}}\par \par \uc2 I started wondering if I could write a program that would create a painting.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/hodlers_cover_sept_12-18.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210919eh9i0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 9/17: BTC, ETH,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , BNB, XRP, SOL, DOT, DOGE, UNI, LUNA\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,837 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is sustaining above its immediate support, but several altcoins are showing signs of profit-booking.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) recovery is facing stiff resistance near $48,500, indicating that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 By combining the popular stock-to-flow Bitcoin price model and the illiquid supply data, analyst William Clemente projects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/new-bitcoin-price-model-suggests-btc-won-t-go-below-39k-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $39,000 to act as a strong floor}}}\uc2  on any declines.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, analysts remain \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bloomberg Intelligence chief analyst Mike McGlone has maintained his target of $100,000 for Bitcoin. McGlone said that a number of different charts underline the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  potential for Bitcoin.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/5f10294b-11a6-4c1c-bf1e-a65110c63661.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Along with Bitcoin, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) is also showing signs of accumulation. Crypto analytics provider IntoTheBlock said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/1-2b-in-ether-withdrawn-from-centralized-exchanges-in-record-daily-outflow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.2 billion worth of Ether was withdrawn}}}\uc2  within a 24-hour period from centralized exchanges on Sept. 16. After a similar occurrence in April, Ether had rallied about 60% in 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Could the top two cryptocurrencies live up to their \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  projections or will crypto markets surprise to the downside? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls are attempting to sustain Bitcoin above the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) ($47,291) while bears are trying to pull the price below it. The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index (RSI) is close to the midpoint, suggesting a range-bound action in the short term.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/bde0eac0-1494-4643-ad42-f8510deed56f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below the moving averages, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the critical support at $42,451.67. A rebound off this level will indicate that bulls are accumulating on dips. That may extend the consolidation between $42,451.67 and $52,920 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off the current level or the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) ($46,256), the bulls will try to push the pair to $50,500 and then to $52,920. The bears are likely to defend this resistance zone aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The next major trending move is likely to begin after bulls drive the price above $52,920 or if bears pull the price below $42,451.67.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) recovery is facing stiff resistance at the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $3,637.14, indicating selling at higher levels. The bears are attempting to sink the price back below the support at $3,377.89.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/60fde7b6-54c4-41da-9e84-1fc598fd1689.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If they succeed, the ETH/USDT could drop to the 50-day SMA ($3,238) and then to the critical support at $3,000. Such a move may result in the formation of a head and shoulder pattern, which will complete on a break and close below $3,000.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate if the price rebounds off the support at $3,377.89 or the 50-day SMA and breaks above $3,676.28. The pair could then retest the local high at $4,027.88.\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint do not indicate a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($2.52) on Sept. 16, suggesting that bears are selling on rallies to this resistance. The bears are currently attempting to pull the price to the 50-day SMA ($2.25).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/ab28a1d8-70dd-4e84-ad50-2fc8cbf8827c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone suggest that bears are in command. If the price sustains below the 50-day SMA, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the next support at $1.94.\par \par \uc2 Such a deep correction will suggest that a short-term top has been made. If bulls want to salvage the uptrend, they will have to push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA. If they do that, the pair could once again rally to $2.80 and then to $2.97.\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to push Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($432) in the past two days, indicating that buying dries up at higher levels. This may have attracted profit-booking from short-term traders who bought at lower levels, anticipating a resumption of the up-move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e8a6acb9-d1bd-4d12-9438-7d68ffee0ee1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is sloping down and the RSI turned down from the midpoint, suggesting advantage to the sellers. If the price sustains below the 50-day SMA, the BNB/USDT pair could drop to the next major support at $340.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated if the bulls push and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA. Such a move will suggest that the bulls have absorbed the supply. The pair could then rise to the overhead resistance at $518.90.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT\par \par \uc2 Ripple ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 20-day EMA ($1.12) on Sept. 16, indicating that bears are defending this level aggressively. The downsloping 20-day EMA and the RSI in the negative zone suggest that the path of least resistance is to the downside.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/54375e7c-e5d7-42d8-8b32-aa7e4b5fe168.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bears sustain the price below the 50-day SMA, the XRP/USDT pair could retest the Sept. 7 intraday low at $0.95. A break and close below this support will open the doors for a deeper correction to $0.75.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the current level or from $0.95, the bulls will again try to push the price above the 20-day EMA. If they succeed, it will suggest that the correction could be over. The pair may then start its northward march toward $1.35.\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT\par \par \uc2 Solana\u8217\'20\'19s (SOL) bounce off the 20-day EMA ($145) on Sept. 14 fizzled out at $166.50 as bears continued to pounce on relief rallies. The price has slipped below the 20-day EMA today, indicating weakness.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/0bd3c59c-e87b-4e6e-a98a-cf1984808d79.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattening 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest that bulls have lost their grip. If bears sustain the price below the 20-day EMA, the SOL/USDT pair could decline to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level at $123.42.\par \par \uc2 This is an important support to watch out for because if it cracks, the pair could plunge to psychological support at $100.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level or rebounds off $123.42, the bulls will try to resume the uptrend. The up-move could face stiff resistance near $170 and then at $200.\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT\par \par \uc2 Polkadot (DOT) turned down from the resistance line on Sept. 15 and dropped close to the 20-day EMA ($32.04) on Sept.. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break below it could pull the price down to the 50-day SMA ($26.36).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/8231217b-c8fc-4d13-b5a6-41b6bb4cd4d1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the moving averages are sloping up, the negative divergence on the RSI warns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum could be slowing down. A break and close below the 50-day SMA could suggest the start of a deeper correction.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to propel the DOT/USDT pair above the resistance line. If they manage to do that, the pair could pick up momentum and rally to $41.40 and then retest the all-time high at $49.78.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/next-stop-85k-for-bitcoin-as-analysts-predict-explosive-q4-for-btc-price-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Next stop $85K for Bitcoin as analysts predict \u8216\'20\'18explosive\u8217\'20\'19 Q4 for BTC price action}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Dogecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been trading below the moving averages for the past few days, the bears have not been able to sink the price to the immediate support at $0.21. This suggests a lack of sellers at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/e3d08407-efda-49ba-b3e4-fd8aa525ef59.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls attempted to push the price above the moving averages today but the bears are in no mood to relent. The downsloping 20-day EMA ($0.26) and the RSI below 42 indicate that sellers have the upper hand.\par \par \uc2 If bears sink the price below $0.21, the DOGE/USDT pair could extend the decline to $0.15. Alternatively, if bulls drive the price above the moving averages, the pair could rise to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 A break and close above this resistance will be the first sign that the correction may be over. The pair could then start its journey toward the overhead resistance at $0.45.\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) surged above the moving averages on Sept. 15 but the bulls could not push the price above the downtrend line, which may have attracted profit-booking by the short-term bulls and shorting by the aggressive bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/a65619ab-2ff2-46a4-808a-ef4598654967.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flat 20-day EMA ($25.72) and the RSI just below 50 indicate a marginal advantage to the bears. If the price sustains below $25, the bears will try to pull the UNI/USDT pair to $23.50 and then to $21. If this support cracks, it will indicate the start of a deeper correction.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off the current level or $23.50, the bulls will again try to drive the price above the downtrend line. If they succeed, the pair could move up to the overhead resistance at $31.41.\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT\par \par \uc2 Terra protocol\u8217\'20\'19s LUNA token rose to $39.77 on Sept. 16 but could not sustain the higher levels as seen from the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. This suggests that traders may be closing their long positions on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2021-09/03a7a201-10a1-43bd-a3a7-4150fed5d874.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LUNA/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will now try to seize the opportunity and sink the price below the 20-day exponential moving average ($33.97). If they manage to do that, the LUNA/USDT pair could decline to the 50-day SMA ($26.26).\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price again rebounds off the 20-day EMA, the pair could rise to $40 and remain range-bound between these two levels for a few more days. A breakout and close above $40 could open the doors for a retest of the all-time high at $45.01.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk. You should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 Market data is provided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hitbtc.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 HitBTC}}}\uc2  exchange.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjEtMDkvMWJmOGQzZmUtN2JjNS00NDkwLWJjNWQtYWM0MWUzYWRiYjA5LmpwZw==.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210917eh9h000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Columns\par \b \uc2 Shanghai Man: China\u8217\'20\'19s version of McJob meme, eCNY airdrops, Canaan\u8217\'20\'19s record revenue\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ben Yorke \par \uc2 891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This weekly roundup of news from Mainland China, Taiwan, and Hong Kong attempts to curate the industrys most important news, including influential projects, changes in the regulatory landscape, and enterprise blockchain integrations.\par \par \uc2 Regulatory noise\par \par \uc2 In this weeks column, the Man in Shanghai is determined to squeeze all of the regulatory noise into one section so as not to waste too much of your time. Lets begin.\par \par \uc2 It wasnt much, just a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/hebei-is-the-latest-china-province-to-wield-the-crypto-crackdown-hammer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning from the Hebei Provincial government}}}\uc2  that it would put an end to cryptocurrency mining in the region. This is largely a non-story since its essentially just a restatement of a national-level policy that went into effect months ago. Hebei was never much of a mining stronghold anyway, so the announcement is more procedural than anything else. Mining operations will continue to move overseas while China goes through its unified push to become carbon neutral.\par \par \uc2 For reference, China has 23 provinces, and close to half have already restated their commitment to the national policy of not tolerating cryptocurrency mining.\par \par \uc2 The Securities Times, a state-owned publication, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/chinese-communist-party-warn-of-nft-hype-bubble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ran a story}}}\uc2  to warn the public about the bubble surrounding nonfungible tokens, or NFTs. This Shenzhen-based publication questioned the real economic value of NFTs, a topic that many of us have wondered about at times. Still, the suspicion hasn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped the trend from spilling into less mainstream art circles, where NFT and metaverse-related events are becoming more and more popular.\par \par \uc2 Selling shovels in a gold rush\par \par \uc2 While mining in China might be difficult, manufacturing mining machines continues to be profitable. Canaan, one of the worlds largest manufacturers of cryptocurrency mining hardware, announced i {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-miner-maker-canaan-records-highest-quarterly-profit-since-2019-ipo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ts highest quarterly profits to date}}}\uc2 . The companys Q2 financials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://canaan.io/1177.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  that the company recorded over $167.5 million in total net revenue. This was likely driven by the sharp increase in prices this spring, leading to an aggressive expansion of mining facilities across the world. The next round of quarterly financials will tell a deeper story, as investors learn how badly China\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive regulations have hurt the industry. Zhang Nangeng, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Canaan said:\par \par \uc2 We delivered a remarkable performance in the second quarter of 2021. Despite unexpected regulatory policy dynamics and Bitcoin price \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we achieved record-high topline results as we delivered a robust 5.9 million Thash/s of computing power to our clients.\par \par \uc2 Rounding up the trading space\par \par \uc2 Volume remained mostly flat on exchanges like Huobi and OKEx, as it has for the last 12 weeks. The last major spike came during the sell-off in early May, around the time Chinese regulators began their crackdown. Over this time, FTX has seen a strong increase in volume, suggesting that some Chinese users might be connecting to exchanges that havent been dominant players in the Chinese trading space.\par \par \uc2 FIL remains popular on Huobi, finishing in the top five on Thursdays 24-hr volume chart. This token has maintained popularity among traders in China, despite being about 50% below its all-time high from earlier this year. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , SOL, and DOT were assets that showed up high on OKEx volume charts, which mirrored global volume distributions. Speaking of Solana, Chinese users on Weibo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://weibo.com/6470674840/Kyf4vmZBD?from=page_1005056470674840_profile&wvr=6&mod=weibotime&type=comment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reacted}}}\uc2  strongly to the network going offline on Wednesday, with some criticizing the networks decentralization. A discussion broke out about whether Ethereums early technical issues were comparable to this event, proving that Solana and Ethereum maxis will disagree in any culture, regardless of the language.\par \par \uc2 Unleashing the eCNY\par \par \uc2 The central bank digital currency created by the Chinese federal bank is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://weibo.com/ttarticle/p/show?id=2309404679571332268177"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being pushed}}}\uc2  out even further, as popular app Meituan is offering roughly $1.50 in eCNY (digital yuan) to users who open a digital wallet and use its services.\par \par \uc2 Meituan is most widely known for its bright yellow food delivery service and shared bikes, which can be found on most city streets. The campaign is meant to encourage low-carbon living and is open to nine pilot cities, including Beijing, Shanghai, Shenzhen and Chengdu.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/3061631772003_.pic_hd-762x1024.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The wallet interface is minimalist and allows users to convert, deposit, and transfer the eCNY\par \par \uc2 The eCNY, which was originally positioned as more of an institutional remittance tool for commercial banks, is now being pushed towards retail users aggressively. Already, large franchises like \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  and Zara display eCNY payment signs at point-of-sale counters across the country. The current digital payment space is dominated by \uc2 WeChat\uc2  Pay and Alipay, but those two will likely have a hard time holding control of market share if the central government is interested in forcing eCNY into competing applications.\par \par \uc2 Ironically, Meituan has a special role in Chinese cryptocurrency meme culture. Token holders often joke they will be forced to work in food delivery whenever the market crashes, leading to the meme below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://miro.medium.com/max/1200/0*PjPSW9oTilUtRfeD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Great Crypto Meme War. There will be a great crypto meme war | by MAO DAO | Jul, 2021 | Medium}}}\par \par \uc2 Meituan\u8217\'20\'19s iconic delivery drivers are the source of many crypto-related {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maodaonft.medium.com/the-great-crypto-meme-war-97a8d40fa23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memes}}}\uc2  during a market crash.\par \par \uc2 At the end of March, Meituan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/meituan-announces-financial-results-for-the-three-months-ended-march-31-2021-301301600.html#:~:text=Meituan%20has%20569.3%20million%20Annual,cities%20and%20counties%20in%20China."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  it had around 570 million users. Other financial apps, including banking apps, have already integrated wallet services into their products.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/MAG-our-man-in-shanghai-5.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020210917eh9h0008k\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Columns\par \b \uc2 Shanghai Man: China\u8217\'20\'19s version of McJob meme, eCNY airdrops, Canaan\u8217\'20\'19s record revenue\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Ben Yorke \par \uc2 894 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2021\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2021. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This weekly roundup of news from Mainland China, Taiwan, and Hong Kong attempts to curate the industrys most important news, including influential projects, changes in the regulatory landscape, and enterprise blockch